.SH rclone copy
Copy files from source to dest, skipping identical files.
.SS Synopsis
Copy the source to the destination.
Does not transfer files that are identical on source and destination,
testing by size and modification time or MD5SUM.
Doesn\(aqt delete files from the destination.
If you want to also delete files from destination, to make it match
source, use the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_sync/
sync
.UE \c
\ command instead.
.PP
Note that it is always the contents of the directory that is synced, not
the directory itself.
So when source:path is a directory, it\(aqs the contents of source:path
that are copied, not the directory name and contents.
.PP
To copy single files, use the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_copyto/
copyto
.UE \c
\ command instead.
.PP
If dest:path doesn\(aqt exist, it is created and the source:path
contents go there.
.PP
For example
.IP
.EX
rclone copy source:sourcepath dest:destpath
.EE
.PP
Let\(aqs say there are two files in sourcepath
.IP
.EX
sourcepath/one.txt
sourcepath/two.txt
.EE
.PP
This copies them to
.IP
.EX
destpath/one.txt
destpath/two.txt
.EE
.PP
Not to
.IP
.EX
destpath/sourcepath/one.txt
destpath/sourcepath/two.txt
.EE
.PP
If you are familiar with \f[CR]rsync\f[R], rclone always works as if you
had written a trailing \f[CR]/\f[R] \- meaning \(dqcopy the contents of
this directory\(dq.
This applies to all commands and whether you are talking about the
source or destination.
.PP
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#no-traverse
\-\-no\-traverse
.UE \c
\ option for controlling whether rclone lists the destination directory
or not.
Supplying this option when copying a small number of files into a large
destination can speed transfers up greatly.
.PP
For example, if you have many files in /path/to/src but only a few of
them change every day, you can copy all the files which have changed
recently very efficiently like this:
.IP
.EX
rclone copy \-\-max\-age 24h \-\-no\-traverse /path/to/src remote:
.EE
.PP
Rclone will sync the modification times of files and directories if the
backend supports it.
If metadata syncing is required then use the \f[CR]\-\-metadata\f[R]
flag.
.PP
Note that the modification time and metadata for the root directory will
\f[B]not\f[R] be synced.
See \c
.UR https://github.com/rclone/rclone/issues/7652
issue #7652
.UE \c
\ for more info.
.PP
\f[B]Note\f[R]: Use the \f[CR]\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-progress\f[R] flag to
view real\-time transfer statistics.
.PP
\f[B]Note\f[R]: Use the \f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R] or the
\f[CR]\-\-interactive\f[R]/\f[CR]\-i\f[R] flag to test without copying
anything.
.SS Logger Flags
The \f[CR]\-\-differ\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-missing\-on\-dst\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-missing\-on\-src\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-match\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-\-error\f[R] flags write paths, one per line, to the file name
(or stdout if it is \f[CR]\-\f[R]) supplied.
What they write is described in the help below.
For example \f[CR]\-\-differ\f[R] will write all paths which are present
on both the source and destination but different.
.PP
The \f[CR]\-\-combined\f[R] flag will write a file (or stdout) which
contains all file paths with a symbol and then a space and then the path
to tell you what happened to it.
These are reminiscent of diff files.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]= path\f[R] means path was found in source and destination and was
identical
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\- path\f[R] means path was missing on the source, so only in the
destination
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]+ path\f[R] means path was missing on the destination, so only in
the source
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]* path\f[R] means path was present in source and destination but
different.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]! path\f[R] means there was an error reading or hashing the source
or dest.
.PP
The \f[CR]\-\-dest\-after\f[R] flag writes a list file using the same
format flags as \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_lsf/#synopsis
\f[CR]lsf\f[R]
.UE \c
\ (including \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_lsf/#synopsis
customizable options for hash, modtime, etc.
.UE \c
) Conceptually it is similar to rsync\(aqs
\f[CR]\-\-itemize\-changes\f[R], but not identical \-\- it should output
an accurate list of what will be on the destination after the command is
finished.
.PP
When the \f[CR]\-\-no\-traverse\f[R] flag is set, all logs involving
files that exist only on the destination will be incomplete or
completely missing.
.PP
Note that these logger flags have a few limitations, and certain
scenarios are not currently supported:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-max\-duration\f[R] / \f[CR]CutoffModeHard\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-compare\-dest\f[R] / \f[CR]\-\-copy\-dest\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
server\-side moves of an entire dir at once
.IP \(bu 2
High\-level retries, because there would be duplicates (use
\f[CR]\-\-retries 1\f[R] to disable)
.IP \(bu 2
Possibly some unusual error scenarios
.PP
Note also that each file is logged during execution, as opposed to
after, so it is most useful as a predictor of what SHOULD happen to each
file (which may or may not match what actually DID).
.IP
.EX
rclone copy source:path dest:path [flags]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
      \-\-absolute                Put a leading / in front of path names
      \-\-combined string         Make a combined report of changes to this file
      \-\-create\-empty\-src\-dirs   Create empty source dirs on destination after copy
      \-\-csv                     Output in CSV format
      \-\-dest\-after string       Report all files that exist on the dest post\-sync
      \-\-differ string           Report all non\-matching files to this file
  \-d, \-\-dir\-slash               Append a slash to directory names (default true)
      \-\-dirs\-only               Only list directories
      \-\-error string            Report all files with errors (hashing or reading) to this file
      \-\-files\-only              Only list files (default true)
  \-F, \-\-format string           Output format \- see lsf help for details (default \(dqp\(dq)
      \-\-hash h                  Use this hash when h is used in the format MD5|SHA\-1|DropboxHash (default \(dqmd5\(dq)
  \-h, \-\-help                    help for copy
      \-\-match string            Report all matching files to this file
      \-\-missing\-on\-dst string   Report all files missing from the destination to this file
      \-\-missing\-on\-src string   Report all files missing from the source to this file
  \-s, \-\-separator string        Separator for the items in the format (default \(dq;\(dq)
  \-t, \-\-timeformat string       Specify a custom time format \- see docs for details (default: 2006\-01\-02 15:04:05)
.EE
.PP
Options shared with other commands are described next.
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/flags/
global flags page
