.SH rclone purge
Remove the path and all of its contents.
.SS Synopsis
Remove the path and all of its contents.
Note that this does not obey include/exclude filters \- everything will
be removed.
Use the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_delete/
delete
.UE \c
\ command if you want to selectively delete files.
To delete empty directories only, use command \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_rmdir/
rmdir
.UE \c
\ or \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_rmdirs/
rmdirs
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
The concurrency of this operation is controlled by the
\f[CR]\-\-checkers\f[R] global flag.
However, some backends will implement this command directly, in which
case \f[CR]\-\-checkers\f[R] will be ignored.
.PP
\f[B]Important\f[R]: Since this can cause data loss, test first with the
\f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R] or the \f[CR]\-\-interactive\f[R]/\f[CR]\-i\f[R]
flag.
