.SH rclone ls
List the objects in the path with size and path.
.SS Synopsis
Lists the objects in the source path to standard output in a human
readable format with size and path.
Recurses by default.
.PP
E.g.
.IP
.EX
$ rclone ls swift:bucket
    60295 bevajer5jef
    90613 canole
    94467 diwogej7
    37600 fubuwic
.EE
.PP
Any of the filtering options can be applied to this command.
.PP
There are several related list commands
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]ls\f[R] to list size and path of objects only
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]lsl\f[R] to list modification time, size and path of objects only
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]lsd\f[R] to list directories only
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]lsf\f[R] to list objects and directories in easy to parse format
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]lsjson\f[R] to list objects and directories in JSON format
.PP
\f[CR]ls\f[R],\f[CR]lsl\f[R],\f[CR]lsd\f[R] are designed to be
human\-readable.
\f[CR]lsf\f[R] is designed to be human and machine\-readable.
\f[CR]lsjson\f[R] is designed to be machine\-readable.
.PP
Note that \f[CR]ls\f[R] and \f[CR]lsl\f[R] recurse by default \- use
\f[CR]\-\-max\-depth 1\f[R] to stop the recursion.
.PP
The other list commands \f[CR]lsd\f[R],\f[CR]lsf\f[R],\f[CR]lsjson\f[R]
do not recurse by default \- use \f[CR]\-R\f[R] to make them recurse.
.PP
List commands prefer a recursive method that uses more memory but fewer
transactions by default.
Use \f[CR]\-\-disable ListR\f[R] to suppress the behavior.
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#fast-list
\f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R]
.UE \c
\ for more details.
.PP
Listing a nonexistent directory will produce an error except for remotes
which can\(aqt have empty directories (e.g.
s3, swift, or gcs \- the bucket\-based remotes).
.IP
.EX
rclone ls remote:path [flags]
.EE
