.SH rclone about
Get quota information from the remote.
.SS Synopsis
Prints quota information about a remote to standard output.
The output is typically used, free, quota and trash contents.
.PP
E.g.
Typical output from \f[CR]rclone about remote:\f[R] is:
.IP
.EX
Total:   17 GiB
Used:    7.444 GiB
Free:    1.315 GiB
Trashed: 100.000 MiB
Other:   8.241 GiB
.EE
.PP
Where the fields are:
.IP \(bu 2
Total: Total size available.
.IP \(bu 2
Used: Total size used.
.IP \(bu 2
Free: Total space available to this user.
.IP \(bu 2
Trashed: Total space used by trash.
.IP \(bu 2
Other: Total amount in other storage (e.g.
Gmail, Google Photos).
.IP \(bu 2
Objects: Total number of objects in the storage.
.PP
All sizes are in number of bytes.
.PP
Applying a \f[CR]\-\-full\f[R] flag to the command prints the bytes in
full, e.g.
.IP
.EX
Total:   18253611008
Used:    7993453766
Free:    1411001220
Trashed: 104857602
Other:   8849156022
.EE
.PP
A \f[CR]\-\-json\f[R] flag generates conveniently machine\-readable
output, e.g.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtotal\(dq: 18253611008,
  \(dqused\(dq: 7993453766,
  \(dqtrashed\(dq: 104857602,
  \(dqother\(dq: 8849156022,
  \(dqfree\(dq: 1411001220
}
.EE
.PP
Not all backends print all fields.
Information is not included if it is not provided by a backend.
Where the value is unlimited it is omitted.
.PP
Some backends does not support the \f[CR]rclone about\f[R] command at
all, see complete list in \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
documentation
.UE \c
\&.
.IP
.EX
rclone about remote: [flags]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
      \-\-full   Full numbers instead of human\-readable
  \-h, \-\-help   help for about
      \-\-json   Format output as JSON
.EE
.PP
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/flags/
global flags page
.UE \c
\ for global options not listed here.
