.PP
The \f[CR]\-\-prefix\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-full\-path\f[R] flags control
the prefix for the files in the archive.
.PP
If the flag \f[CR]\-\-full\-path\f[R] is set then the files will have
the full source path as the prefix.
.PP
If the flag \f[CR]\-\-prefix=<value>\f[R] is set then the files will
have \f[CR]<value>\f[R] as prefix.
It\(aqs possible to create invalid file names with
\f[CR]\-\-prefix=<value>\f[R] so use with caution.
Flag \f[CR]\-\-prefix\f[R] has priority over \f[CR]\-\-full\-path\f[R].
.PP
Given a directory \f[CR]/sourcedir\f[R] with the following:
.IP
.EX
file1.txt
dir1/file2.txt
.EE
.PP
Running the command
\f[CR]rclone archive create /sourcedir /dest.tar.gz\f[R] will make an
archive with the contents:
.IP
.EX
file1.txt
dir1/
dir1/file2.txt
.EE
.PP
Running the command
\f[CR]rclone archive create \-\-full\-path /sourcedir /dest.tar.gz\f[R]
will make an archive with the contents:
.IP
.EX
sourcedir/file1.txt
sourcedir/dir1/
sourcedir/dir1/file2.txt
.EE
.PP
Running the command
\f[CR]rclone archive create \-\-prefix=my_new_path /sourcedir /dest.tar.gz\f[R]
will make an archive with the contents:
.IP
.EX
my_new_path/file1.txt
my_new_path/dir1/
my_new_path/dir1/file2.txt
.EE
.IP
.EX
rclone archive create [flags] <source> [<destination>]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
      \-\-format string   Create the archive with format or guess from extension.
      \-\-full\-path       Set prefix for files in archive to source path
  \-h, \-\-help            help for create
      \-\-prefix string   Set prefix for files in archive to entered value or source path
.EE
.PP
