.SH rclone backend
Run a backend\-specific command.
.SS Synopsis
This runs a backend\-specific command.
The commands themselves (except for \(dqhelp\(dq and \(dqfeatures\(dq)
are defined by the backends and you should see the backend docs for
definitions.
.PP
You can discover what commands a backend implements by using
.IP
.EX
rclone backend help remote:
rclone backend help <backendname>
.EE
.PP
You can also discover information about the backend using (see \c
.UR https://rclone.org/rc/#operations-fsinfo
operations/fsinfo
.UE \c
\ in the remote control docs for more info).
.IP
.EX
rclone backend features remote:
.EE
.PP
Pass options to the backend command with \-o.
This should be key=value or key, e.g.:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend stats remote:path stats \-o format=json \-o long
.EE
.PP
Pass arguments to the backend by placing them on the end of the line
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup remote:path file1 file2 file3
.EE
.PP
Note to run these commands on a running backend then see \c
.UR https://rclone.org/rc/#backend-command
backend/command
.UE \c
\ in the rc docs.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend <command> remote:path [opts] <args> [flags]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
  \-h, \-\-help                 help for backend
      \-\-json                 Always output in JSON format
  \-o, \-\-option stringArray   Option in the form name=value or name
.EE
