.SH rclone config unset
Unset options in an existing remote.
.SS Synopsis
Remove one or more options from an existing remote.
The options to remove should be passed in as a list of key names.
.PP
For example, to remove the \f[CR]client_id\f[R] and
\f[CR]client_secret\f[R] options from a remote of name myremote you
would do:
.IP
.EX
rclone config unset myremote client_id client_secret
.EE
.PP
This removes the keys from the config file entirely, which is different
from setting them to an empty string with \f[CR]config update\f[R].
Removing a key restores rclone\(aqs default behaviour for that option,
whereas setting it to an empty string overrides the default with an
empty value.
.PP
You can\(aqt unset the \f[CR]type\f[R] of a remote \- use
\f[CR]config delete\f[R] to remove the whole remote instead.
.IP
.EX
rclone config unset name [key]+ [flags]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
  \-h, \-\-help   help for unset
.EE
