.SH rclone rcat
Copies standard input to file on remote.
.SS Synopsis
Reads from standard input (stdin) and copies it to a single remote file.
.IP
.EX
echo \(dqhello world\(dq | rclone rcat remote:path/to/file
ffmpeg \- | rclone rcat remote:path/to/file
.EE
.PP
If the remote file already exists, it will be overwritten.
.PP
rcat will try to upload small files in a single request, which is
usually more efficient than the streaming/chunked upload endpoints,
which use multiple requests.
Exact behaviour depends on the remote.
What is considered a small file may be set through
\f[CR]\-\-streaming\-upload\-cutoff\f[R].
Uploading only starts after the cutoff is reached or if the file ends
before that.
The data must fit into RAM.
The cutoff needs to be small enough to adhere the limits of your remote,
please see there.
Generally speaking, setting this cutoff too high will decrease your
performance.
.PP
Use the \f[CR]\-\-size\f[R] flag to preallocate the file in advance at
the remote end and actually stream it, even if remote backend doesn\(aqt
support streaming.
.PP
\f[CR]\-\-size\f[R] should be the exact size of the input stream in
bytes.
If the size of the stream is different in length to the
\f[CR]\-\-size\f[R] passed in then the transfer will likely fail.
.PP
Note that the upload cannot be retried because the data is not stored.
If the backend supports multipart uploading then individual chunks can
be retried.
If you need to transfer a lot of data, you may be better off caching it
locally and then \f[CR]rclone move\f[R] it to the destination which can
use retries.
.IP
.EX
rclone rcat remote:path [flags]
.EE
.SS Options
.IP
.EX
  \-h, \-\-help       help for rcat
      \-\-size int   File size hint to preallocate (default \-1)
.EE
.PP
Options shared with other commands are described next.
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/flags/
global flags page
.UE \c
\ for global options not listed here.
.SS Important Options
Important flags useful for most commands
.IP
.EX
  \-n, \-\-dry\-run         Do a trial run with no permanent changes
  \-i, \-\-interactive     Enable interactive mode
  \-v, \-\-verbose count   Print lots more stuff (repeat for more)
.EE
