.SH rclone rmdirs
Remove empty directories under the path.
.SS Synopsis
This recursively removes any empty directories (including directories
that only contain empty directories), that it finds under the path.
The root path itself will also be removed if it is empty, unless you
supply the \f[CR]\-\-leave\-root\f[R] flag.
.PP
Use command \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_rmdir/
rmdir
.UE \c
\ to delete just the empty directory given by path, not recurse.
.PP
This is useful for tidying up remotes that rclone has left a lot of
empty directories in.
For example the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_delete/
delete
.UE \c
\ command will delete files but leave the directory structure (unless
used with option \f[CR]\-\-rmdirs\f[R]).
.PP
This will delete \f[CR]\-\-checkers\f[R] directories concurrently so if
you have thousands of empty directories consider increasing this number.
.PP
To delete a path and any objects in it, use the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_purge/
purge
.UE \c
\ command.
.IP
.EX
rclone rmdirs remote:path [flags]
.EE
