.SS rc/error: This returns an error
This returns an error with the input as part of its error string.
Useful for testing error handling.
.PP
\f[B]Authentication is not required for this call.\f[R]
.SS rc/fatal: This returns an fatal error
This returns an error with the input as part of its error string.
Useful for testing error handling.
.SS rc/list: List all the registered remote control commands
This lists all the registered remote control commands as a JSON map in
the commands response.
.PP
\f[B]Authentication is not required for this call.\f[R]
.SS rc/noop: Echo the input to the output parameters
This echoes the input parameters to the output parameters for testing
purposes.
It can be used to check that rclone is still alive and to check that
parameter passing is working properly.
.PP
\f[B]Authentication is not required for this call.\f[R]
.SS rc/noopauth: Echo the input to the output parameters requiring auth
This echoes the input parameters to the output parameters for testing
purposes.
It can be used to check that rclone is still alive and to check that
parameter passing is working properly.
.SS rc/panic: This returns an error by panicking
This returns an error with the input as part of its error string.
Useful for testing error handling.
.SS serve/list: Show running servers
Show running servers with IDs.
.PP
This takes no parameters and returns
.IP \(bu 2
list: list of running serve commands
.PP
Each list element will have
.IP \(bu 2
id: ID of the server
.IP \(bu 2
addr: address the server is running on
.IP \(bu 2
params: parameters used to start the server
.PP
Eg
.IP
.EX
rclone rc serve/list
.EE
.PP
Returns
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqlist\(dq: [
        {
            \(dqaddr\(dq: \(dq[::]:4321\(dq,
            \(dqid\(dq: \(dqnfs\-ffc2a4e5\(dq,
            \(dqparams\(dq: {
                \(dqfs\(dq: \(dqremote:\(dq,
                \(dqopt\(dq: {
                    \(dqListenAddr\(dq: \(dq:4321\(dq
                },
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqnfs\(dq,
                \(dqvfsOpt\(dq: {
                    \(dqCacheMode\(dq: \(dqfull\(dq
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}
.EE
.SS serve/start: Create a new server
Create a new server with the specified parameters.
.PP
This takes the following parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]type\f[R] \- type of server: \f[CR]http\f[R], \f[CR]webdav\f[R],
\f[CR]ftp\f[R], \f[CR]sftp\f[R], \f[CR]nfs\f[R], etc.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]fs\f[R] \- remote storage path to serve
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]addr\f[R] \- the ip:port to run the server on, eg \(dq:1234\(dq or
\(dqlocalhost:1234\(dq
.PP
Other parameters are as described in the documentation for the relevant
\c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_serve/
rclone serve
.UE \c
\ command line options.
To translate a command line option to an rc parameter, remove the
leading \f[CR]\-\-\f[R] and replace \f[CR]\-\f[R] with \f[CR]_\f[R], so
\f[CR]\-\-vfs\-cache\-mode\f[R] becomes \f[CR]vfs_cache_mode\f[R].
.PP
Option parameters (such as VFS, proxy, and protocol\-specific options)
can be passed flat at the top level of the parameter map or inside
nested JSON objects under the \f[CR]vfsOpt\f[R], \f[CR]proxyOpt\f[R],
and \f[CR]opt\f[R] keys (e.g.
\f[CR]vfsOpt=\(aq{\(dqCacheMode\(dq: 2}\(aq\f[R],
\f[CR]proxyOpt=\(aq{\(dqAuthProxy\(dq: \(dqhttp://127.0.0.1:8080\(dq}\(aq\f[R]).
If both flat parameters and nested blocks are supplied, the parameters
in the nested blocks will take precedence.
Note that global parameters must be set with \f[CR]_config\f[R] and
\f[CR]_filter\f[R] as described above.
.PP
Examples:
.IP
.EX
rclone rc serve/start type=nfs fs=remote: addr=:4321 vfs_cache_mode=full
rclone rc serve/start \-\-json \(aq{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqnfs\(dq,\(dqfs\(dq:\(dqremote:\(dq,\(dqaddr\(dq:\(dq:1234\(dq,\(dqvfs_cache_mode\(dq:\(dqfull\(dq}\(aq
rclone rc serve/start type=webdav fs=remote: vfsOpt=\(aq{\(dqCacheMode\(dq: 2}\(aq proxyOpt=\(aq{\(dqAuthProxy\(dq: \(dqhttp://127.0.0.1:8080\(dq}\(aq
.EE
.PP
This will give the reply
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqaddr\(dq: \(dq[::]:4321\(dq, \f[B]//\f[R] \f[B]Address\f[R] \f[B]the\f[R] \f[B]server\f[R] \f[B]was\f[R] \f[B]started\f[R] \f[B]on\f[R]
    \(dqid\(dq: \(dqnfs\-ecfc6852\(dq \f[B]//\f[R] \f[B]Unique\f[R] \f[B]identifier\f[R] \f[B]for\f[R] \f[B]the\f[R] \f[B]server\f[R] \f[B]instance\f[R]
}
.EE
.PP
Or an error if it failed to start.
.PP
Stop the server with \f[CR]serve/stop\f[R] and list the running servers
with \f[CR]serve/list\f[R].
.SS serve/stop: Unserve selected active serve
Stops a running \f[CR]serve\f[R] instance by ID.
.PP
This takes the following parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
id: as returned by serve/start
.PP
This will give an empty response if successful or an error if not.
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
rclone rc serve/stop id=12345
.EE
.SS serve/stopall: Stop all active servers
Stop all active servers.
.PP
This will stop all active servers.
.IP
.EX
rclone rc serve/stopall
.EE
.SS serve/types: Show all possible serve types
This shows all possible serve types and returns them as a list.
.PP
This takes no parameters and returns
.IP \(bu 2
types: list of serve types, eg \(dqnfs\(dq, \(dqsftp\(dq, etc
.PP
The serve types are strings like \(dqserve\(dq, \(dqserve2\(dq,
\(dqcserve\(dq and can be passed to serve/start as the serveType
parameter.
.PP
Eg
.IP
.EX
rclone rc serve/types
.EE
.PP
Returns
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqtypes\(dq: [
        \(dqhttp\(dq,
        \(dqsftp\(dq,
        \(dqnfs\(dq
    ]
}
.EE
.SS sync/bisync: Perform bidirectional synchronization between two paths.
.PP
This takes the following parameters:
.IP \(bu 2
path1 (required) \- (string) a remote directory string e.g.
\f[CR]drive:path1\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
path2 (required) \- (string) a remote directory string e.g.
\f[CR]drive:path2\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
dryRun \- (bool) dry\-run mode
.IP \(bu 2
backupDir1 \- (string) \-\-backup\-dir for Path1.
Must be a non\-overlapping path on the same remote.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
backupDir2 \- (string) \-\-backup\-dir for Path2.
Must be a non\-overlapping path on the same remote.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
checkAccess \- (bool) Ensure expected RCLONE_TEST files are found on
both Path1 and Path2 filesystems, else abort.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
checkFilename \- (string) Filename for \-\-check\-access (default:
RCLONE_TEST)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
checkSync \- (string) Controls comparison of final listings:
true|false|only (default: true)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
compare \- (string) Comma\-separated list of bisync\-specific compare
options ex.
\(aqsize,modtime,checksum\(aq (default: \(aqsize,modtime\(aq)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
conflictLoser \- (ConflictLoserAction) Action to take on the loser of a
sync conflict (when there is a winner) or on both files (when there is
no winner): , num, pathname, delete (default: num)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
conflictResolve \- (string) Automatically resolve conflicts by
preferring the version that is: none, path1, path2, newer, older,
larger, smaller (default: none)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
conflictSuffix \- (string) Suffix to use when renaming a
\-\-conflict\-loser.
Can be either one string or two comma\-separated strings to assign
different suffixes to Path1/Path2.
(default: \(aqconflict\(aq)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
createEmptySrcDirs \- (bool) Sync creation and deletion of empty
directories.
(Not compatible with \-\-remove\-empty\-dirs)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
downloadHash \- (bool) Compute hash by downloading when otherwise
unavailable.
(warning: may be slow and use lots of data!)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
filtersFile \- (string) Read filtering patterns from a file
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
force \- (bool) Bypass \-\-max\-delete safety check and run the sync.
Consider using with \-\-verbose
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
ignoreListingChecksum \- (bool) Do not use checksums for listings (add
\-\-ignore\- checksum to additionally skip post\-copy checksum checks)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
maxLock \- (Duration) Consider lock files older than this to be expired
(default: 0 (never expire)) (minimum: 2m)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
noCleanup \- (bool) Retain working files (useful for troubleshooting and
testing).
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
noSlowHash \- (bool) Ignore listing checksums only on backends where
they are slow
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
recover \- (bool) Automatically recover from interruptions without
requiring \-\- resync.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
removeEmptyDirs \- (bool) Remove ALL empty directories at the final
cleanup step.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
resilient \- (bool) Allow future runs to retry after certain
less\-serious errors, instead of requiring \-\-resync.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
resync \- (bool) Performs the resync run.
Equivalent to \-\-resync\-mode path1.
Consider using \-\-verbose or \-\-dry\-run first.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
resyncMode \- (string) During resync, prefer the version that is: path1,
path2, newer, older, larger, smaller (default: path1 if \-\-resync,
otherwise none for no resync.)
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
slowHashSyncOnly \- (bool) Ignore slow checksums for listings and
deltas, but still consider them during sync calls.
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
workdir \- (string) Use custom working dir \- useful for testing.
(default: /home/ncw/.cache/rclone/bisync)
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_bisync/
bisync command help
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/bisync/
full bisync description
.UE \c
\ for more information.
