DavideRossi/upback
.UE \c
.PP
Bisync adopts the differential synchronization technique, which is based
on keeping history of changes performed by both synchronizing sides.
See the \f[I]Dual Shadow Method\f[R] section in \c
.UR https://neil.fraser.name/writing/sync/
Neil Fraser\(aqs article
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
Also note a number of academic publications by \c
.UR http://www.cis.upenn.edu/%7Ebcpierce/papers/index.shtml#File%20Synchronization
Benjamin Pierce
.UE \c
\ about \f[I]Unison\f[R] and synchronization in general.
