.SS Limitations
\f[CR]rclone about\f[R] is not supported by the 1Fichier backend.
Backends without this capability cannot determine free space for an
rclone mount or use policy \f[CR]mfs\f[R] (most free space) as a member
of an rclone union remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
List of backends that do not support rclone about
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_about/
rclone about
.UE \c
\&.
.SH Alias
The \f[CR]alias\f[R] remote provides a new name for another remote.
.PP
Paths may be as deep as required or a local path, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:directory/subdirectory\f[R] or
\f[CR]/directory/subdirectory\f[R].
.PP
During the initial setup with \f[CR]rclone config\f[R] you will specify
the target remote.
The target remote can either be a local path or another remote.
.PP
Subfolders can be used in target remote.
Assume an alias remote named \f[CR]backup\f[R] with the target
\f[CR]mydrive:private/backup\f[R].
Invoking \f[CR]rclone mkdir backup:desktop\f[R] is exactly the same as
invoking \f[CR]rclone mkdir mydrive:private/backup/desktop\f[R].
.PP
There will be no special handling of paths containing \f[CR]..\f[R]
segments.
Invoking \f[CR]rclone mkdir backup:../desktop\f[R] is exactly the same
as invoking \f[CR]rclone mkdir mydrive:private/backup/../desktop\f[R].
The empty path is not allowed as a remote.
To alias the current directory use \f[CR].\f[R] instead.
.PP
The target remote can also be a \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#connection-strings
connection string
.UE \c
\&.
This can be used to modify the config of a remote for different uses,
e.g.
the alias \f[CR]myDriveTrash\f[R] with the target remote
\f[CR]myDrive,trashed_only:\f[R] can be used to only show the trashed
files in \f[CR]myDrive\f[R].
.SS Configuration
Here is an example of how to make an alias called \f[CR]remote\f[R] for
local folder.
First run:
