.SS \-\-s3\-use\-already\-exists
Set if rclone should report BucketAlreadyExists errors on bucket
creation.
.PP
At some point during the evolution of the s3 protocol, AWS started
returning an \f[CR]AlreadyOwnedByYou\f[R] error when attempting to
create a bucket that the user already owned, rather than a
\f[CR]BucketAlreadyExists\f[R] error.
.PP
Unfortunately exactly what has been implemented by s3 clones is a little
inconsistent, some return \f[CR]AlreadyOwnedByYou\f[R], some return
\f[CR]BucketAlreadyExists\f[R] and some return no error at all.
.PP
This is important to rclone because it ensures the bucket exists by
creating it on quite a lot of operations (unless
\f[CR]\-\-s3\-no\-check\-bucket\f[R] is used).
.PP
If rclone knows the provider can return \f[CR]AlreadyOwnedByYou\f[R] or
returns no error then it can report \f[CR]BucketAlreadyExists\f[R]
errors when the user attempts to create a bucket not owned by them.
Otherwise rclone ignores the \f[CR]BucketAlreadyExists\f[R] error which
can lead to confusion.
.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers rclone
knows about \- please make a bug report if not.
.PP
