.SS Rclone Serve S3
Rclone can serve any remote over the S3 protocol.
For details see the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_serve_s3/
rclone serve s3
.UE \c
\ documentation.
.PP
For example, to serve \f[CR]remote:path\f[R] over s3, run the server
like this:
.IP
.EX
rclone serve s3 \-\-auth\-key ACCESS_KEY_ID,SECRET_ACCESS_KEY remote:path
.EE
.PP
This will be compatible with an rclone remote which is defined like
this:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][serves3]\f[R]
type = s3
provider = Rclone
endpoint = http://127.0.0.1:8080/
access_key_id = ACCESS_KEY_ID
secret_access_key = SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
use_multipart_uploads = \f[B]false\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Note that setting \f[CR]use_multipart_uploads = false\f[R] is to work
around \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_serve_s3/#bugs
a bug
.UE \c
\ which will be fixed in due course.
