.PP
\c
.UR https://www.scaleway.com/en/glacier-cold-storage/
Scaleway Glacier
.UE \c
\ is the low\-cost S3 Glacier alternative from Scaleway and it works the
same way as on S3 by accepting the \(dqGLACIER\(dq
\f[CR]storage_class\f[R].
So you can configure your remote with the
\f[CR]storage_class = GLACIER\f[R] option to upload directly to Scaleway
Glacier.
Don\(aqt forget that in this state you can\(aqt read files back after,
you will need to restore them to \(dqSTANDARD\(dq storage_class first
before being able to read them (see \(dqrestore\(dq section above)
.SS Scality
\c
.UR https://www.scality.com/
Scality
.UE \c
\ RING and ARTESCA both expose an S3\-compatible object storage API that
works with rclone using \f[CR]s3\f[R] as the type and \f[CR]Scality\f[R]
as the provider.
.PP
Both products are S3 clones, so you always need to set the
\f[CR]endpoint\f[R] to the S3 API of your deployment (the S3 Connector
service on RING, or the S3 data\-service endpoint on ARTESCA).
The \f[CR]Scality\f[R] provider uses path\-style addressing
(\f[CR]endpoint/bucket/key\f[R]) which is supported out of the box and
does not require any wildcard/virtual\-host DNS entries.
.PP
Get your access key, secret key and endpoint from your Scality
administrator (on ARTESCA these are created per account under
\f[I]Identity > Accounts\f[R] in the UI; on RING they are created with
\f[CR]vaultclient\f[R] or the S3 Console).
.PP
