.SS Backend quirks
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-chunk\-size\f[R] is forced to be 64 MiB or greater.
This will use more memory than the default of 5 MiB.
.IP \(bu 2
Server side copy is disabled as it isn\(aqt currently supported in the
gateway.
.IP \(bu 2
GetTier and SetTier are not supported.
.SS Backend bugs
Due to \c
.UR https://github.com/storj/gateway-mt/issues/39
issue #39
.UE \c
\ uploading multipart files via the S3 gateway causes them to lose their
metadata.
For rclone\(aqs purpose this means that the modification time is not
stored, nor is any MD5SUM (if one is available from the source).
.PP
This has the following consequences:
.IP \(bu 2
Using \f[CR]rclone rcat\f[R] will fail as the metadata doesn\(aqt match
after upload
.IP \(bu 2
Uploading files with \f[CR]rclone mount\f[R] will fail for the same
reason
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
This can worked around by using \f[CR]\-\-vfs\-cache\-mode writes\f[R]
or \f[CR]\-\-vfs\-cache\-mode full\f[R] or setting
\f[CR]\-\-s3\-upload\-cutoff\f[R] large
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Files uploaded via a multipart upload won\(aqt have their modtimes
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
This will mean that \f[CR]rclone sync\f[R] will likely keep trying to
upload files bigger than \f[CR]\-\-s3\-upload\-cutoff\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
This can be worked around with \f[CR]\-\-checksum\f[R] or
\f[CR]\-\-size\-only\f[R] or setting \f[CR]\-\-s3\-upload\-cutoff\f[R]
large
.IP \(bu 2
The maximum value for \f[CR]\-\-s3\-upload\-cutoff\f[R] is 5GiB though
.RE
.PP
One general purpose workaround is to set
\f[CR]\-\-s3\-upload\-cutoff 5G\f[R].
This means that rclone will upload files smaller than 5GiB as single
parts.
Note that this can be set in the config file with
\f[CR]upload_cutoff = 5G\f[R] or configured in the advanced settings.
If you regularly transfer files larger than 5G then using
\f[CR]\-\-checksum\f[R] or \f[CR]\-\-size\-only\f[R] in
\f[CR]rclone sync\f[R] is the recommended workaround.
.SS Comparison with the native protocol
Use the the native protocol to take advantage of client\-side encryption
as well as to achieve the best possible download performance.
Uploads will be erasure\-coded locally, thus a 1gb upload will result in
2.68gb of data being uploaded to storage nodes across the network.
.PP
Use this backend and the S3 compatible Hosted Gateway to increase upload
performance and reduce the load on your systems and network.
Uploads will be encrypted and erasure\-coded server\-side, thus a 1GB
upload will result in only in 1GB of data being uploaded to storage
nodes across the network.
.PP
For more detailed comparison please check the documentation of the storj
backend.
