.SS lifecycle
Read or set the lifecycle for a bucket.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend lifecycle remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command can be used to read or set the lifecycle for a bucket.
.PP
To show the current lifecycle rules:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend lifecycle b2:bucket
.EE
.PP
This will dump something like this showing the lifecycle rules.
.IP
.EX
[
    {
        \(dqdaysFromHidingToDeleting\(dq: 1,
        \(dqdaysFromUploadingToHiding\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
        \(dqdaysFromStartingToCancelingUnfinishedLargeFiles\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
        \(dqfileNamePrefix\(dq: \(dq\(dq
    }
]
.EE
.PP
If there are no lifecycle rules (the default) then it will just return
\f[CR][]\f[R].
.PP
To reset the current lifecycle rules:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend lifecycle b2:bucket \-o daysFromHidingToDeleting=30
rclone backend lifecycle b2:bucket \-o daysFromUploadingToHiding=5 \-o daysFromHidingToDeleting=1
.EE
.PP
This will run and then print the new lifecycle rules as above.
.PP
Rclone only lets you set lifecycles for the whole bucket with the
fileNamePrefix = \(dq\(dq.
.PP
You can\(aqt disable versioning with B2.
The best you can do is to set the daysFromHidingToDeleting to 1 day.
You can enable hard_delete in the config also which will mean deletions
won\(aqt cause versions but overwrites will still cause versions to be
made.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend lifecycle b2:bucket \-o daysFromHidingToDeleting=1
.EE
.PP
See: \c
.UR https://www.backblaze.com/docs/cloud-storage-lifecycle-rules
.UE \c
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqdaysFromHidingToDeleting\(dq: After a file has been hidden for this
many days it is deleted.
0 is off.
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqdaysFromStartingToCancelingUnfinishedLargeFiles\(dq: Cancels any
unfinished large file versions after this many days.
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqdaysFromUploadingToHiding\(dq: This many days after uploading a file
is hidden.
.SS cleanup
Remove unfinished large file uploads.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command removes unfinished large file uploads of age greater than
max\-age, which defaults to 24 hours.
.PP
Note that you can use \-\-interactive/\-i or \-\-dry\-run with this
command to see what it would do.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup b2:bucket/path/to/object
rclone backend cleanup \-o max\-age=7w b2:bucket/path/to/object
.EE
.PP
Durations are parsed as per the rest of rclone, 2h, 7d, 7w etc.
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqmax\-age\(dq: Max age of upload to delete.
.SS cleanup\-hidden
Remove old versions of files.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup\-hidden remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command removes any old hidden versions of files.
.PP
Note that you can use \-\-interactive/\-i or \-\-dry\-run with this
command to see what it would do.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup\-hidden b2:bucket/path/to/dir
.EE
.SS Limitations
\f[CR]rclone about\f[R] is not supported by the B2 backend.
Backends without this capability cannot determine free space for an
rclone mount or use policy \f[CR]mfs\f[R] (most free space) as a member
of an rclone union remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
List of backends that do not support rclone about
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_about/
rclone about
.UE \c
\&.
.SH Box
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:path\f[R]
.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:directory/subdirectory\f[R].
.PP
The initial setup for Box involves getting a token from Box which you
can do either in your browser, or with a config.json downloaded from Box
to use JWT authentication.
\f[CR]rclone config\f[R] walks you through it.
