\- \-1 (default) \(em recommended; equivalent to level 5.
\- 0 \(em turns off compression.
\- 1\(en9 \(em increase compression at the cost of speed. Going past 6 generally offers very little return.
 
ZSTD (levels 0 to 4):
\- 0 \(em turns off compression entirely.
\- 1 \(em fastest compression with the lowest ratio.
