.SH Combine
The \f[CR]combine\f[R] backend joins remotes together into a single
directory tree.
.PP
For example you might have a remote for images on one provider:
.IP
.EX
$ rclone tree s3:imagesbucket
/
├── image1.jpg
└── image2.jpg
.EE
.PP
And a remote for files on another:
.IP
.EX
$ rclone tree drive:important/files
/
├── file1.txt
└── file2.txt
.EE
.PP
The \f[CR]combine\f[R] backend can join these together into a synthetic
directory structure like this:
.IP
.EX
$ rclone tree combined:
/
├── files
│   ├── file1.txt
│   └── file2.txt
└── images
    ├── image1.jpg
    └── image2.jpg
.EE
.PP
You\(aqd do this by specifying an \f[CR]upstreams\f[R] parameter in the
config like this
.IP
.EX
upstreams = images=s3:imagesbucket files=drive:important/files
.EE
.PP
During the initial setup with \f[CR]rclone config\f[R] you will specify
the upstreams remotes as a space separated list.
The upstream remotes can either be a local paths or other remotes.
