.SS Configuring for Google Drive Shared Drives
Rclone has a convenience feature for making a combine backend for all
the shared drives you have access to.
.PP
Assuming your main (non shared drive) Google drive remote is called
\f[CR]drive:\f[R] you would run
.IP
.EX
rclone backend \-o config drives drive:
.EE
.PP
This would produce something like this:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][My Drive]\f[R]
type = alias
remote = drive,team_drive=0ABCDEF\-01234567890,root_folder_id=:

\f[B][Test Drive]\f[R]
type = alias
remote = drive,team_drive=0ABCDEFabcdefghijkl,root_folder_id=:

\f[B][AllDrives]\f[R]
type = combine
upstreams = \(dqMy Drive=My Drive:\(dq \(dqTest Drive=Test Drive:\(dq
.EE
.PP
If you then add that config to your config file (find it with
\f[CR]rclone config file\f[R]) then you can access all the shared drives
in one place with the \f[CR]AllDrives:\f[R] remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/drive/#drives
the Google Drive docs
.UE \c
\ for full info.
