Required: false
.SS Limitations
Note that Dropbox is case insensitive so you can\(aqt have a file called
\(dqHello.doc\(dq and one called \(dqhello.doc\(dq.
.PP
There are some file names such as \f[CR]thumbs.db\f[R] which Dropbox
can\(aqt store.
There is a full list of them in the \c
.UR https://www.dropbox.com/en/help/145
\(dqIgnored Files\(dq section of this document
.UE \c
\&.
Rclone will issue an error message
\f[CR]File name disallowed \- not uploading\f[R] if it attempts to
upload one of those file names, but the sync won\(aqt fail.
.PP
Some errors may occur if you try to sync copyright\-protected files
because Dropbox has its own \c
.UR https://techcrunch.com/2014/03/30/how-dropbox-knows-when-youre-sharing-copyrighted-stuff-without-actually-looking-at-your-stuff/
copyright detector
.UE \c
\ that prevents this sort of file being downloaded.
This will return the error
\f[CR]ERROR : /path/to/your/file: Failed to copy: failed to open source object: path/restricted_content/.\f[R]
.PP
If you have more than 10,000 files in a directory then
\f[CR]rclone purge dropbox:dir\f[R] will return the error
\f[CR]Failed to purge: There are too many files involved in this operation\f[R].
As a work\-around do an \f[CR]rclone delete dropbox:dir\f[R] followed by
an \f[CR]rclone rmdir dropbox:dir\f[R].
.PP
When using \f[CR]rclone link\f[R] you\(aqll need to set
\f[CR]\-\-expire\f[R] if using a non\-personal account otherwise the
visibility may not be correct.
(Note that \f[CR]\-\-expire\f[R] isn\(aqt supported on personal
accounts).
See the \c
.UR https://forum.rclone.org/t/rclone-link-dropbox-permissions/23211
forum discussion
.UE \c
\ and the \c
.UR https://github.com/dropbox/dropbox-sdk-go-unofficial/issues/75
dropbox SDK issue
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
Modification times for Dropbox Paper documents are not exact, and may
not change for some period after the document is edited.
To make sure you get recent changes in a sync, either wait an hour or
so, or use \f[CR]\-\-ignore\-times\f[R] to force a full sync.
.SS Get your own Dropbox App ID
When you use rclone with Dropbox in its default configuration you are
using rclone\(aqs App ID.
This is shared between all the rclone users.
.PP
Here is how to create your own Dropbox App ID for rclone:
.IP "1." 3
Log into the \c
.UR https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps/create
Dropbox App console
.UE \c
\ with your Dropbox Account (It need not to be the same account as the
Dropbox you want to access)
.IP "2." 3
Choose an API => Usually this should be \f[CR]Dropbox API\f[R]
.IP "3." 3
Choose the type of access you want to use => \f[CR]Full Dropbox\f[R] or
\f[CR]App Folder\f[R].
If you want to use Team Folders, \f[CR]Full Dropbox\f[R] is required (\c
.UR https://www.dropboxforum.com/t5/Dropbox-API-Support-Feedback/How-to-create-team-folder-inside-my-app-s-folder/m-p/601005/highlight/true#M27911
see here
.UE \c
).
.IP "4." 3
Name your App.
The app name is global, so you can\(aqt use \f[CR]rclone\f[R] for
example
.IP "5." 3
Click the button \f[CR]Create App\f[R]
.IP "6." 3
Switch to the \f[CR]Permissions\f[R] tab.
Enable at least the following permissions: \f[CR]account_info.read\f[R],
\f[CR]files.metadata.write\f[R], \f[CR]files.content.write\f[R],
\f[CR]files.content.read\f[R], \f[CR]sharing.write\f[R].
The \f[CR]files.metadata.read\f[R] and \f[CR]sharing.read\f[R]
checkboxes will be marked too.
Click \f[CR]Submit\f[R]
.IP "7." 3
Switch to the \f[CR]Settings\f[R] tab.
Fill \f[CR]OAuth2 \- Redirect URIs\f[R] as
\f[CR]http://localhost:53682/\f[R] and click on \f[CR]Add\f[R]
.IP "8." 3
Find the \f[CR]App key\f[R] and \f[CR]App secret\f[R] values on the
\f[CR]Settings\f[R] tab.
Use these values in rclone config to add a new remote or edit an
existing remote.
The \f[CR]App key\f[R] setting corresponds to \f[CR]client_id\f[R] in
rclone config, the \f[CR]App secret\f[R] corresponds to
\f[CR]client_secret\f[R]
.SH Enterprise File Fabric
This backend supports \c
.UR https://storagemadeeasy.com/about/
Storage Made Easy\(aqs Enterprise File Fabric™
.UE \c
\ which provides a software solution to integrate and unify File and
Object Storage accessible through a global file system.
.SS Configuration
The initial setup for the Enterprise File Fabric backend involves
getting a token from the Enterprise File Fabric which you need to do in
your browser.
\f[CR]rclone config\f[R] walks you through it.
.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \f[CR]remote\f[R].
First run:
.IP
.EX
rclone config
.EE
.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:
.IP
.EX
