.PP
Invalid UTF\-8 bytes will also be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
Files.com treats the replacements \f[CR]／\f[R] and \f[CR]＼\f[R] as if
they were \f[CR]/\f[R] and \f[CR]\(rs\f[R], and the names \f[CR]．\f[R]
and \f[CR]．．\f[R] as if they were \f[CR].\f[R] and \f[CR]..\f[R], and
rejects them with \f[CR]Invalid path\f[R].
This means that files with \f[CR]/\f[R] or \f[CR]\(rs\f[R] in their
names, or which are called \f[CR].\f[R] or \f[CR]..\f[R], can\(aqt be
stored on Files.com.
.SS Hashes
In December 2024 \f[CR]files.com\f[R] started \c
.UR https://www.files.com/blog/2024/11/01/new-modern-checksum-options-now-available-with-opt
supporting more checksums
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
However if you want hashes you \f[B]must\f[R] enable them in your site
by visiting the \(dqFile Integrity\(dq section in \(dqData
Governance\(dq to configure your settings and select the checksum
algorithms that meet your requirements.
.PP
Rclone currently only support CRC32 and MD5 for use in syncing but
selecting more checksums will not affect rclone\(aqs operations.
.PP
For use with rclone, selecting at least MD5 is recommended so rclone can
do an end to end integrity check.
