.SS Limitations
FTP servers acting as rclone remotes must support \f[CR]passive\f[R]
mode.
The mode cannot be configured as \f[CR]passive\f[R] is the only
supported one.
Rclone\(aqs FTP implementation is not compatible with \f[CR]active\f[R]
mode as \c
.UR https://github.com/jlaffaye/ftp/issues/29
the library it uses doesn\(aqt support it
.UE \c
\&.
This will likely never be supported due to security concerns.
.PP
Rclone\(aqs FTP backend does not support any checksums but can compare
file sizes.
.PP
\f[CR]rclone about\f[R] is not supported by the FTP backend.
Backends without this capability cannot determine free space for an
rclone mount or use policy \f[CR]mfs\f[R] (most free space) as a member
of an rclone union remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
List of backends that do not support rclone about
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_about/
rclone about
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
The implementation of : \f[CR]\-\-dump headers\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-dump bodies\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dump auth\f[R] for debugging
isn\(aqt the same as for rclone HTTP based backends \- it has less fine
grained control.
.PP
\f[CR]\-\-timeout\f[R] isn\(aqt supported (but \f[CR]\-\-contimeout\f[R]
is).
.PP
\f[CR]\-\-bind\f[R] isn\(aqt supported.
.PP
Rclone\(aqs FTP backend could support server\-side move but does not at
present.
.PP
The \f[CR]ftp_proxy\f[R] environment variable is not currently
supported.
.SS Modification times
File modification time (timestamps) is supported to 1 second resolution
for major FTP servers: ProFTPd, PureFTPd, VsFTPd, and FileZilla FTP
server.
The \f[CR]VsFTPd\f[R] server has non\-standard implementation of time
related protocol commands and needs a special configuration setting:
\f[CR]writing_mdtm = true\f[R].
.PP
Support for precise file time with other FTP servers varies depending on
what protocol extensions they advertise.
If all the \f[CR]MLSD\f[R], \f[CR]MDTM\f[R] and \f[CR]MFTM\f[R]
extensions are present, rclone will use them together to provide precise
time.
Otherwise the times you see on the FTP server through rclone are those
of the last file upload.
.PP
You can use the following command to check whether rclone can use
precise time with your FTP server:
\f[CR]rclone backend features your_ftp_remote:\f[R] (the trailing colon
is important).
Look for the number in the line tagged by \f[CR]Precision\f[R]
designating the remote time precision expressed as nanoseconds.
A value of \f[CR]1000000000\f[R] means that file time precision of 1
second is available.
A value of \f[CR]3153600000000000000\f[R] (or another large number)
means \(dqunsupported\(dq.
.SH Gofile
\c
.UR https://gofile.io
Gofile
.UE \c
\ is a content storage and distribution platform.
Its aim is to provide as much service as possible for free or at a very
low price.
.PP
The initial setup for Gofile involves logging in to the web interface
and going to the \(dqMy Profile\(dq section.
Copy the \(dqAccount API token\(dq for use in the config file.
.PP
Note that if you wish to connect rclone to Gofile you will need a
premium account.
