.SS Public Links
Gofile supports \f[CR]rclone link\f[R] to make public links to files or
directories.
If you specify a directory it will download as a \f[CR]zip\f[R] file.
You can use the \f[CR]\-\-expire\f[R] flag to specify the time the link
should be valid.
Note that \f[CR]rclone link \-\-unlink\f[R] removes all the public links
for a file.
.SS Root folder ID
You can set the \f[CR]root_folder_id\f[R] for rclone.
This is the directory (identified by its \f[CR]Folder ID\f[R]) that
rclone considers to be the root of your Gofile drive.
.PP
Normally you will leave this blank and rclone will determine the correct
root to use itself and fill in the value in the config file.
.PP
However you can set this to restrict rclone to a specific folder
hierarchy.
.PP
In order to do this you will have to find the \f[CR]Folder ID\f[R] of
the directory you wish rclone to display.
.PP
You can do this with rclone
.IP
.EX
$ rclone lsf \-Fip \-\-dirs\-only remote:
d6341f53\-ee65\-4f29\-9f59\-d11e8070b2a0;Files/
f4f5c9b8\-6ece\-478b\-b03e\-4538edfe5a1c;Photos/
d50e356c\-29ca\-4b27\-a3a7\-494d91026e04;Videos/
.EE
.PP
The ID to use is the part before the \f[CR];\f[R] so you could set
.IP
.EX
root_folder_id = d6341f53\-ee65\-4f29\-9f59\-d11e8070b2a0
.EE
.PP
To restrict rclone to the \f[CR]Files\f[R] directory.
