.EE
.SS Getting your own Client ID and Secret
When you use rclone with Huawei Drive in its default configuration you
are using rclone\(aqs client_id.
This is shared between all the rclone users.
There is a global rate limit on the number of queries per second that
each client_id can do set by Huawei.
.PP
It is strongly recommended to use your own client ID as the default
rclone ID is heavily used.
If you have multiple services running, it is recommended to use a
separate client ID for each service to avoid rate limiting issues.
.PP
Here is how to create your own Huawei Drive client ID for rclone:
.PP
Follow the detailed guides for complete setup instructions:
.IP \(bu 2
\c
.UR https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/HMSCore-Guides/web-preparations-0000001050050891
Huawei HMS Core Web App Preparations
.UE \c
.IP \(bu 2
\c
.UR https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/HMSCore-Guides/server-preparations-0000001050185577#section194911701377
Huawei HMS Core Server Preparations
.UE \c
.PP
Rclone uses the web application access method to connect to Huawei
Drive.
Before starting, you need to implement quick login authorization through
Huawei Account Open Service.
With user authorization credentials, rclone can call Huawei Cloud Drive
Service APIs.
.SS Create Server Application
Before accessing Drive service, developers need to create a server
application first.
For details, please refer to the WEB Application Access Development
Preparation section in the \(dqHuawei Account Service Development
Guide\(dq.
.SS Enable Drive Application Switch
.IP "1." 3
Log in to AppGallery Connect with your Huawei account.
.IP "2." 3
Create a project or select an existing project.
.IP "3." 3
Add a web application to the project.
.IP "4." 3
Open \(dqProject settings\(dq for the application and copy the OAuth 2.0
Client ID and Client Secret from the \(dqGeneral\(dq tab.
.IP "5." 3
Open \(dqAPI Management\(dq for the project and enable \(dqCloud
Drive\(dq.
.IP "6." 3
Add \f[CR]http://127.0.0.1:53682/\f[R] as a redirect URI for the OAuth
2.0 Client ID.
.PP
The older Huawei Developer Console may show some of the same credential
information, but AppGallery Connect is the place to create the project,
application, API permission, and redirect URI used by rclone.
.SS Sign Huawei Cloud Drive Privacy Notice and User Agreement
Guide users to visit \c
.UR https://cloud.huawei.com/
.UE \c
\&.
First\-time users need to sign the agreement before they can use Huawei
Cloud Drive Service.
.SS Application Access to Obtain Authentication Credential Access Token
Applications accessing Drive should use authentication credential Access
Token.
For specific acquisition methods, please refer to the WEB Application
Access Development Guide section in the \(dqHuawei Account Service
Development Guide\(dq.
.PP
Key steps summary:
.IP "1." 3
Create or select a project in AppGallery Connect.
.IP "2." 3
Add a web application to the project.
.IP "3." 3
Enable Cloud Drive in API Management.
.IP "4." 3
Configure \f[CR]http://127.0.0.1:53682/\f[R] as the OAuth redirect URI.
.IP "5." 3
Copy the OAuth 2.0 Client ID and Client Secret from the application.
.IP "6." 3
Provide the client ID and client secret to rclone during configuration.
.SS Scopes
Rclone uses the following OAuth2 scopes when accessing Huawei Drive:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive\f[R] \- Full access to Huawei
Drive files (excluding application data folder)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.file\f[R] \- Access to files
created by the application
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]openid\f[R] \- OpenID Connect authentication
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]profile\f[R] \- Access to basic profile information
.PP
The \f[CR]drive.file\f[R] scope is included in the default set used by
rclone.
.PP
Alternative scopes available (not used by rclone by default):
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.appdata\f[R] \- Access to
application data folder
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.readonly\f[R] \- Read\-only
access to file metadata and content
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.metadata\f[R] \- Read/write
access to file metadata only
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]https://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.metadata.readonly\f[R] \-
Read\-only access to file metadata only
.PP
The default scopes provide read/write access to all files in your Huawei
Drive.
.SS Modification times and hashes
Huawei Drive does not support setting modification times.
The API always uses server\-side timestamps, so file modification times
from the source are not preserved during upload.
Modification times are available as read\-only metadata
(\f[CR]mtime\f[R], \f[CR]btime\f[R]).
.PP
Hash algorithm SHA256 is supported for file integrity verification.
.SS Restricted filename characters
Huawei Drive has strict restrictions on file and directory names:
.IP \(bu 2
Cannot contain: \f[CR]< > | : \(dq * ? / \(rs\f[R] or emoji characters
.IP \(bu 2
Cannot be exactly \f[CR]. ..\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum length: 250 bytes
.IP \(bu 2
Single quotes must be escaped with \f[CR]\(rs\(aq\f[R] in API calls
.PP
These restrictions are handled by rclone\(aqs encoding:
.IP \(bu 2
Backslashes \f[CR]\(rs\f[R] are encoded
.IP \(bu 2
Invalid UTF\-8 sequences are encoded
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
Right\-side spaces are encoded
.PP
Invalid characters will be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
\ according to the encoding settings.
.SS Resumable uploads
Huawei Drive supports resumable uploads for files larger than the upload
cutoff (default 20MB).
Files are uploaded in chunks which allows for recovery from network
interruptions.
.SS File size limits
The maximum file size for Huawei Drive is 50 GiB.
.SS Quota information
To view your current quota you can use the
\f[CR]rclone about remote:\f[R] command which will display your usage
and quota information.
