.SS Limitations
Huawei Drive has some rate limiting which may cause rclone to slow down
transfers to avoid hitting the limits.
.SS File name restrictions
.IP \(bu 2
File names cannot contain: \f[CR]< > | : \(dq * ? / \(rs\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
File names cannot be exactly \f[CR]. ..\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum file name length is 250 bytes
.IP \(bu 2
Some unicode characters including emojis are not supported
.SS API rate limits
Huawei Drive imposes API rate limits.
Rclone automatically handles these by backing off when limits are hit.
.SS OAuth2 token expiry
.IP \(bu 2
Access tokens expire after 1 hour
.IP \(bu 2
Refresh tokens expire after 180 days
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.IP \(bu 2
Rclone will automatically refresh tokens as needed
.SS File size limits
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum file size is 50 GiB
.IP \(bu 2
Files larger than this cannot be uploaded
.SS Upload behavior
.IP \(bu 2
Files smaller than \f[CR]upload_cutoff\f[R] (default 20MB) are uploaded
in a single request using content or multipart method
.IP \(bu 2
Larger files are uploaded using resumable uploads with configurable
chunk size
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum single chunk size for resumable uploads is 64MB
.IP \(bu 2
Resumable uploads support automatic retry on network errors
.IP \(bu 2
SHA256 hash verification is supported for uploaded files
.SS Server\-side operations
.IP \(bu 2
Server\-side copy: Files can be copied within Huawei Drive without
downloading and re\-uploading
.IP \(bu 2
Server\-side move: Files and directories can be moved/renamed on the
server side
.IP \(bu 2
Directory move: Entire directories can be moved with a single API call
.SS Directory operations
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei Drive supports creating empty directories
.IP \(bu 2
Recursive listing is supported via \f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R] for
efficient directory traversal
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei Drive has a special \(dqapplicationData\(dq folder for
app\-specific data (not accessible via rclone\(aqs default
configuration)
.SS Error handling
Common errors and their meanings:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]401 Unauthorized\f[R]: Invalid credentials or expired token
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]403 Forbidden\f[R]: Usually indicates insufficient permissions or
API quota exceeded
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]404 Not Found\f[R]: File or directory does not exist
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]409 Conflict\f[R]: Directory already exists
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]429 Too Many Requests\f[R]: API rate limit exceeded, rclone will
automatically retry
.SS Performance tuning
For better performance:
.IP \(bu 2
Increase \f[CR]\-\-transfers\f[R] for concurrent operations (default is
4)
.IP \(bu 2
Adjust \f[CR]chunk_size\f[R] based on your network speed and file sizes
.IP \(bu 2
Use \f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R] for operations on directories with many
files to reduce API calls
.SS Making backups
Huawei Drive is suitable for backups with some considerations:
.IP \(bu 2
Use \f[CR]rclone sync\f[R] rather than \f[CR]rclone copy\f[R] to
maintain exact directory structure
.IP \(bu 2
Consider using \f[CR]\-\-backup\-dir\f[R] to preserve deleted files
.IP \(bu 2
Verify transfers with \f[CR]\-\-checksum\f[R] flag for critical data
.IP \(bu 2
Be aware of the 50 GiB file size limit for individual files
.SS Supported features
Huawei Drive supports the following rclone features:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Copy\f[R] \- Server\-side copy of files
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Move\f[R] \- Server\-side move/rename of files
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]DirMove\f[R] \- Server\-side move of directories
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]ListR\f[R] \- Recursive listing for \f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]About\f[R] \- Storage quota information
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Purge\f[R] \- Delete directory and all contents
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CleanUp\f[R] \- Empty the trash
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]UserInfo\f[R] \- Get user account information
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Metadata\f[R] \- Read and write file metadata/properties
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]ChangeNotify\f[R] \- Poll for remote changes (used by
\f[CR]rclone mount\f[R] and \f[CR]rclone rc vfs/poll\-interval\f[R])
.SS Integration with other services
Huawei Drive can be used as a backend for various rclone operations:
.IP \(bu 2
Mount as a local filesystem using \f[CR]rclone mount\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over HTTP using \f[CR]rclone serve http\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over FTP using \f[CR]rclone serve ftp\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over WebDAV using \f[CR]rclone serve webdav\f[R]
.PP
Note that some operations may be slower than local storage due to API
limitations and network latency.
