.SS Setting up your own HDFS instance for testing
You may start with a \c
.UR https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/stable/hadoop-project-dist/hadoop-common/SingleCluster.html
manual setup
.UE \c
\ or use the docker image from the tests:
.PP
If you want to build the docker image
.IP
.EX
git clone https://github.com/rclone/rclone.git
cd rclone/fstest/testserver/images/test\-hdfs
docker build \-\-rm \-t rclone/test\-hdfs .
.EE
.PP
Or you can just use the latest one pushed
.IP
.EX
docker run \-\-rm \-\-name \(dqrclone\-hdfs\(dq \-p 127.0.0.1:9866:9866 \-p 127.0.0.1:8020:8020 \-\-hostname \(dqrclone\-hdfs\(dq rclone/test\-hdfs
.EE
.PP
\f[B]NB\f[R] it need few seconds to startup.
.PP
For this docker image the remote needs to be configured like this:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][remote]\f[R]
type = hdfs
namenode = 127.0.0.1:8020
username = root
.EE
.PP
You can stop this image with \f[CR]docker kill rclone\-hdfs\f[R]
(\f[B]NB\f[R] it does not use volumes, so all data uploaded will be
lost.)
