.EE
.SS iCloud Photos
The iCloud Drive backend also supports accessing iCloud Photos by
setting the \f[CR]service\f[R] option to \f[CR]photos\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
rclone lsd iclouddrive: \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos
.EE
.PP
This presents a read\-only hierarchy rooted at photo libraries:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Level 1\f[R]: Photo libraries \(em your personal library
(\f[CR]PrimarySync\f[R]) and any Shared Photo Library
(\f[CR]SharedSync\-XXXX\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Level 2+\f[R]: Albums and folders within a library, nested
recursively as in Apple Photos
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Leaf level\f[R]: Photos/videos within an album, including Live
Photo \f[CR].MOV\f[R] companions
.PP
Examples:
.IP
.EX
# List libraries
rclone lsd iclouddrive: \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos

# List albums in your primary library
rclone lsd iclouddrive:PrimarySync/ \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos

# List photos in an album
rclone ls iclouddrive:PrimarySync/All\(rs Photos/ \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos

# Download a photo
rclone copy iclouddrive:PrimarySync/Favorites/IMG_0001.HEIC /tmp/ \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos
.EE
.PP
You can either:
.IP \(bu 2
set \f[CR]service = photos\f[R] in \f[CR]rclone config\f[R] for a
dedicated Photos remote
.IP \(bu 2
keep \f[CR]service = drive\f[R] and pass
\f[CR]\-\-iclouddrive\-service photos\f[R] when needed
.SS Metadata
With \f[CR]\-\-metadata\f[R], Photos entries expose these read\-only
metadata keys:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]width\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]height\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]added\-time\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]favorite\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]hidden\f[R]
.PP
These metadata keys are only available when \f[CR]service = photos\f[R].
.SS Caching
iCloud Photos caches album listings to disk for fast subsequent access.
On the first run, listing a large album uses parallel
\f[CR]startRank\f[R] partitions to fetch pages concurrently.
After that, a lightweight change check (\(ti200ms) determines whether
the cache is still valid.
.PP
Cache location:
\f[CR]\(ti/.cache/rclone/iclouddrive\-photos/<remote>/<zone>/\f[R]
.PP
To clear the cache: delete that directory or run
\f[CR]rclone config reconnect\f[R].
.SS FUSE mounts
For mounting iCloud Photos via \f[CR]rclone mount\f[R], the following
flags are recommended:
.IP
.EX
rclone mount remote: /mnt/photos \(rs
    \-\-iclouddrive\-service photos \(rs
    \-\-vfs\-refresh \(rs
    \-\-dir\-cache\-time 1h \(rs
    \-\-vfs\-cache\-mode full \(rs
    \-\-attr\-timeout 1m \(rs
    \-\-read\-only
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-vfs\-refresh\f[R] pre\-warms directory caches in the
background on mount start so that albums are ready when you browse them
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-dir\-cache\-time 1h\f[R] extends the in\-memory cache lifetime
beyond the default 5 minutes (change detection is fast, so this is safe)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-vfs\-cache\-mode full\f[R] caches downloaded photos and videos
to local disk for fast repeated access
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-attr\-timeout 1m\f[R] reduces kernel attribute lookups (safe
because the backend is read\-only)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-read\-only\f[R] prevents confusing write errors
.PP
The first listing of a very large album (e.g.
75,000 items in \(dqAll Photos\(dq) can take several minutes due to API
pagination limits.
This happens once \(em subsequent listings use the disk cache.
.SS Limitations
iCloud Photos is read\-only.
Upload, delete, rename, and move operations are not supported.
.SS Advanced Data Protection
Advanced Data Protection is supported.
.PP
On iPhone, Settings \f[CR]>\f[R] Apple Account \f[CR]>\f[R] iCloud
\f[CR]>\f[R] \(aqAccess iCloud Data on the Web\(aq must be ON.
.PP
If ADP is enabled on your account, rclone requests PCS cookies after
2FA.
Apple may require approval on a trusted device before those cookies are
issued.
.SS Troubleshooting
.SS PCS cookie errors with ADP
If you see \f[CR]Missing PCS cookies from the request\f[R] or a
\f[CR]requestPCS:\f[R] error, the ADP approval flow did not complete
successfully.
.PP
Check that \(aqAccess iCloud Data on the Web\(aq is enabled and approve
any prompt on your trusted device.
.PP
Then run \f[CR]rclone reconnect remote:\f[R].
.PP
If the remote still has stale auth state, clear the \f[CR]cookies\f[R]
and \f[CR]trust_token\f[R] fields in the config, or delete and recreate
the remote.
