.SS Limitations
Note that Jottacloud is case insensitive so you can\(aqt have a file
called \(dqHello.doc\(dq and one called \(dqhello.doc\(dq.
.PP
There are quite a few characters that can\(aqt be in Jottacloud file
names.
Rclone will map these names to and from an identical looking unicode
equivalent.
For example if a file has a ?
in it will be mapped to ？ instead.
.PP
Jottacloud only supports filenames up to 255 characters in length.
.SS Troubleshooting
Jottacloud exhibits some inconsistent behaviours regarding deleted files
and folders which may cause Copy, Move and DirMove operations to
previously deleted paths to fail.
Emptying the trash should help in such cases.
.SH Koofr
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:path\f[R]
.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:directory/subdirectory\f[R].
.SS Configuration
The initial setup for Koofr involves creating an application password
for rclone.
You can do that by opening the Koofr \c
.UR https://app.koofr.net/app/admin/preferences/password
web application
.UE \c
, giving the password a nice name like \f[CR]rclone\f[R] and clicking on
generate.
.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \f[CR]koofr\f[R].
First run:
.IP
.EX
rclone config
.EE
.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:
.IP
.EX
