.SS Custom upload headers
You can set custom upload headers with the \f[CR]\-\-header\-upload\f[R]
flag.
.IP \(bu 2
Cache\-Control
.IP \(bu 2
Content\-Disposition
.IP \(bu 2
Content\-Encoding
.IP \(bu 2
Content\-Language
.IP \(bu 2
Content\-Type
.IP \(bu 2
X\-MS\-Tags
.PP
Eg \f[CR]\-\-header\-upload \(dqContent\-Type: text/potato\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\-\-header\-upload \(dqX\-MS\-Tags: foo=bar\(dq\f[R].
.SS Limitations
MD5 sums are only uploaded with chunked files if the source has an MD5
sum.
This will always be the case for a local to azure copy.
.PP
\f[CR]rclone about\f[R] is not supported by the Microsoft Azure Blob
storage backend.
Backends without this capability cannot determine free space for an
rclone mount or use policy \f[CR]mfs\f[R] (most free space) as a member
of an rclone union remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
List of backends that do not support rclone about
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_about/
rclone about
.UE \c
\&.
.SS Azure Storage Emulator Support
You can run rclone with the storage emulator (usually
\f[I]azurite\f[R]).
.PP
To do this, just set up a new remote with \f[CR]rclone config\f[R]
following the instructions in the introduction and set
\f[CR]use_emulator\f[R] in the advanced settings as \f[CR]true\f[R].
You do not need to provide a default account name nor an account key.
But you can override them in the \f[CR]account\f[R] and \f[CR]key\f[R]
options.
(Prior to v1.61 they were hard coded to \f[I]azurite\f[R]\(aqs
\f[CR]devstoreaccount1\f[R].)
.PP
Also, if you want to access a storage emulator instance running on a
different machine, you can override the \f[CR]endpoint\f[R] parameter in
the advanced settings, setting it to
\f[CR]http(s)://<host>:<port>/devstoreaccount1\f[R] (e.g.
\f[CR]http://10.254.2.5:10000/devstoreaccount1\f[R]).
.SH Microsoft Azure Files Storage
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:\f[R] You may put subdirectories in
too, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:path/to/dir\f[R].
.SS Configuration
Here is an example of making a Microsoft Azure Files Storage
configuration.
For a remote called \f[CR]remote\f[R].
First run:
.IP
.EX
rclone config
.EE
.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:
.IP
.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
n) New remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/s/q> n
