.SS Getting your own Client ID and Key
rclone uses a default Client ID when talking to OneDrive, unless a
custom \f[CR]client_id\f[R] is specified in the config.
The default Client ID and Key are shared by all rclone users when
performing requests.
.PP
You may choose to create and use your own Client ID, in case the default
one does not work well for you.
For example, you might see throttling.
.SS Creating Client ID for OneDrive Personal
To create your own Client ID, please follow these steps:
.IP "1." 3
Open \c
.UR https://portal.azure.com/?quickstart=true#view/Microsoft_AAD_IAM/ActiveDirectoryMenuBlade/~/Overview
.UE \c
\ and then under the \f[CR]Add\f[R] menu click
\f[CR]App registration\f[R].
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
If you have not created an Azure account, you will be prompted to.
This is free, but you need to provide a phone number, address, and
credit card for identity verification.
.RE
.IP "2." 3
Enter a name for your app, choose account type
\f[CR]Accounts in any organizational directory (Any Azure AD directory \- Multitenant) and personal Microsoft accounts (e.g. Skype, Xbox)\f[R],
select \f[CR]Web\f[R] in \f[CR]Redirect URI\f[R], then type (do not copy
and paste) \f[CR]http://localhost:53682/\f[R] and click Register.
Copy and keep the \f[CR]Application (client) ID\f[R] under the app name
for later use.
.IP "3." 3
Under \f[CR]manage\f[R] select \f[CR]Certificates & secrets\f[R], click
\f[CR]New client secret\f[R].
Enter a description (can be anything) and set \f[CR]Expires\f[R] to 24
months.
Copy and keep that secret \f[I]Value\f[R] for later use (you
\f[I]won\(aqt\f[R] be able to see this value afterwards).
.IP "4." 3
Under \f[CR]manage\f[R] select \f[CR]API permissions\f[R], click
\f[CR]Add a permission\f[R] and select \f[CR]Microsoft Graph\f[R] then
select \f[CR]delegated permissions\f[R].
.IP "5." 3
Search and select the following permissions: \f[CR]Files.Read\f[R],
\f[CR]Files.ReadWrite\f[R], \f[CR]Files.Read.All\f[R],
\f[CR]Files.ReadWrite.All\f[R], \f[CR]offline_access\f[R],
\f[CR]User.Read\f[R] and \f[CR]Sites.Read.All\f[R] (if custom access
scopes are configured, select the permissions accordingly).
Once selected click \f[CR]Add permissions\f[R] at the bottom.
.PP
Now the application is complete.
Run \f[CR]rclone config\f[R] to create or edit a OneDrive remote.
Supply the app ID and password as Client ID and Secret, respectively.
rclone will walk you through the remaining steps.
.PP
The access_scopes option allows you to configure the permissions
requested by rclone.
See \c
.UR https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/permissions-reference#files-permissions
Microsoft Docs
.UE \c
\ for more information about the different scopes.
.PP
The \f[CR]Sites.Read.All\f[R] permission is required if you need to \c
.UR https://github.com/rclone/rclone/pull/5883
search SharePoint sites when configuring the remote
.UE \c
\&.
However, if that permission is not assigned, you need to exclude
\f[CR]Sites.Read.All\f[R] from your access scopes or set
\f[CR]disable_site_permission\f[R] option to true in the advanced
options.
.SS Creating Client ID for OneDrive Business
The steps for OneDrive Personal may or may not work for OneDrive
Business, depending on the security settings of the organization.
A common error is that the publisher of the App is not verified.
.PP
You may try to \c
.UR https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/develop/publisher-verification-overview
verify you account
.UE \c
, or try to limit the App to your organization only, as shown below.
.IP "1." 3
Make sure to create the App with your business account.
.IP "2." 3
Follow the steps above to create an App.
However, we need a different account type here:
\f[CR]Accounts in this organizational directory only (*** \- Single tenant)\f[R].
Note that you can also change the account type after creating the App.
.IP "3." 3
Find the \c
.UR https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/fundamentals/active-directory-how-to-find-tenant
tenant ID
.UE \c
\ of your organization.
.IP "4." 3
In the rclone config, set \f[CR]auth_url\f[R] to
\f[CR]https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID/oauth2/v2.0/authorize\f[R].
.IP "5." 3
In the rclone config, set \f[CR]token_url\f[R] to
\f[CR]https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID/oauth2/v2.0/token\f[R].
.PP
Note: If you have a special region, you may need a different host in
step 4 and 5.
Here are \c
.UR https://github.com/rclone/rclone/blob/bc23bf11db1c78c6ebbf8ea538fbebf7058b4176/backend/onedrive/onedrive.go#L86
some hints
.UE \c
\&.
.SS Using OAuth Client Credential flow
OAuth Client Credential flow will allow rclone to use permissions
directly associated with the Azure AD Enterprise application, rather
that adopting the context of an Azure AD user account.
.PP
This flow can be enabled by following the steps below:
.IP "1." 3
Create the Enterprise App registration in the Azure AD portal and obtain
a Client ID and Client Secret as described above.
.IP "2." 3
Ensure that the application has the appropriate permissions and they are
assigned as \f[I]Application Permissions\f[R]
.IP "3." 3
Configure the remote, ensuring that \f[I]Client ID\f[R] and \f[I]Client
Secret\f[R] are entered correctly.
.IP "4." 3
In the \f[I]Advanced Config\f[R] section, enter \f[CR]true\f[R] for
\f[CR]client_credentials\f[R] and in the \f[CR]tenant\f[R] section enter
the tenant ID.
.PP
When it comes to choosing the type of the connection work with the
client credentials flow.
In particular the \(dqonedrive\(dq option does not work.
You can use the \(dqsharepoint\(dq option or if that does not find the
correct drive ID type it in manually with the \(dqdriveid\(dq option.
.PP
To back up any user\(aqs data using this flow, grant your Azure AD
application the necessary Microsoft Graph \f[I]Application
permissions\f[R] (such as \f[CR]Files.Read.All\f[R],
\f[CR]Sites.Read.All\f[R] and/or \f[CR]Sites.Selected\f[R]).
With these permissions, rclone can access drives across the tenant, but
it needs to know \f[I]which user or drive\f[R] you want.
Supply a specific \f[CR]drive_id\f[R] corresponding to that user\(aqs
OneDrive, or a SharePoint site ID for SharePoint libraries.
You can obtain a user\(aqs drive ID using Microsoft Graph (e.g.
\f[CR]/users/{userUPN}/drive\f[R]) and then configure it in rclone.
Once the correct drive ID is provided, rclone will back up that
user\(aqs data using the app\-only token without requiring their
credentials.
.PP
\f[B]NOTE\f[R] Assigning permissions directly to the application means
that anyone with the \f[I]Client ID\f[R] and \f[I]Client Secret\f[R] can
access your OneDrive files.
Take care to safeguard these credentials.
.SS Non\-admin access to Business OneDrive
If you do not have admin access to your organization\(aqs OneDrive for
Business, you can still connect by manually providing the SharePoint
tenant URL and drive ID.
This works by overriding the base API URL from the standard Microsoft
Graph endpoint to the SharePoint API endpoint.
.SS Steps to manually obtain credentials
.IP "1." 3
Open your browser and navigate to
\f[CR]https://[your\-tenant].sharepoint.com/\f[R]
.IP "2." 3
Open Developer Tools (press F12) and go to the \f[B]Network\f[R] tab.
.IP "3." 3
Search for \f[CR]driveAccessToken\f[R] in the network requests.
.IP "4." 3
Extract the following information from the response:
.RS 4
.IP
.EX
\(dq.driveUrl\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dq{tenant_url}/v2.0/drives/{drive_id}\(dq\f[B],\f[R]
\(dq.driveAccessToken\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dqaccess_token={access_token}\(dq
.EE
.PP
In some guest access scenarios SharePoint may also expose a matching
v2.1 URL and token pair:
.IP
.EX
\(dq.driveUrlV21\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dq{tenant_url}/v2.1/drives/{drive_id}\(dq\f[B],\f[R]
\(dq.driveAccessTokenV21\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dqaccess_token={access_token}\(dq
.EE
.RE
.SS Rclone configuration
Use the extracted values to configure your remote:
.IP
.EX
type = onedrive
token = {\(dqaccess_token\(dq:\(dq{access_token}\(dq,\(dqtoken_type\(dq:\(dqBearer\(dq,\(dqrefresh_token\(dq:\(dq\(dq,\(dqexpiry\(dq:\(dq2045\-12\-31T23:59:59Z\(dq}
drive_id = {drive_id}
tenant_url = {tenant_url}
drive_type = business
.EE
.PP
If you use a v2.1 token, set the matching SharePoint API version:
.IP
.EX
tenant_api_version = v2.1
.EE
.PP
If \f[CR]tenant_api_version\f[R] is omitted, rclone defaults to
\f[CR]v2.0\f[R].
.PP
Since the exact expiry time cannot be determined from web traffic, set
the expiry to a future date.
Note that the token will eventually expire and you will need to repeat
the process to obtain a new one.
.SS Modification times and hashes
OneDrive allows modification times to be set on objects accurate to 1
second.
These will be used to detect whether objects need syncing or not.
.PP
OneDrive Personal, OneDrive for Business and Sharepoint Server support
\c
.UR https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/onedrive/developer/code-snippets/quickxorhash
QuickXorHash
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
Before rclone 1.62 the default hash for Onedrive Personal was
\f[CR]SHA1\f[R].
For rclone 1.62 and above the default for all Onedrive backends is
\f[CR]QuickXorHash\f[R].
.PP
Starting from July 2023 \f[CR]SHA1\f[R] support is being phased out in
Onedrive Personal in favour of \f[CR]QuickXorHash\f[R].
If necessary the \f[CR]\-\-onedrive\-hash\-type\f[R] flag (or
\f[CR]hash_type\f[R] config option) can be used to select
\f[CR]SHA1\f[R] during the transition period if this is important your
workflow.
.PP
For all types of OneDrive you can use the \f[CR]\-\-checksum\f[R] flag.
.SS \-\-fast\-list
This remote supports \f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R] which allows you to use
fewer transactions in exchange for more memory.
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#fast-list
rclone docs
.UE \c
\ for more details.
.PP
This must be enabled with the \f[CR]\-\-onedrive\-delta\f[R] flag (or
\f[CR]delta = true\f[R] in the config file) as it can cause performance
degradation.
.PP
It does this by using the delta listing facilities of OneDrive which
returns all the files in the remote very efficiently.
This is much more efficient than listing directories recursively and is
Microsoft\(aqs recommended way of reading all the file information from
a drive.
.PP
This can be useful with \f[CR]rclone mount\f[R] and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/rc/#vfs-refresh
rclone rc vfs/refresh recursive=true
.UE \c
) to very quickly fill the mount with information about all the files.
.PP
Rclone asks for the delta listing of the directory being listed.
Some drives only support delta listings from the root of the drive, in
which case rclone lists the whole drive and discards the files outside
of the directory you are using, which is increasingly inefficient the
further away from the root you get.
.PP
Some commands (like \f[CR]rclone lsf \-R\f[R]) will use \f[CR]ListR\f[R]
by default \- you can turn this off with \f[CR]\-\-disable ListR\f[R] if
you need to.
