.SS Metadata
OneDrive supports System Metadata (not User Metadata, as of this
writing) for both files and directories.
Much of the metadata is read\-only, and there are some differences
between OneDrive Personal and Business (see table below for details).
.PP
Permissions are also supported, if
\f[CR]\-\-onedrive\-metadata\-permissions\f[R] is set.
The accepted values for \f[CR]\-\-onedrive\-metadata\-permissions\f[R]
are \(dq\f[CR]read\f[R]\(dq, \(dq\f[CR]write\f[R]\(dq,
\(dq\f[CR]read,write\f[R]\(dq, and \(dq\f[CR]off\f[R]\(dq (the default).
\(dq\f[CR]write\f[R]\(dq supports adding new permissions, updating the
\(dqrole\(dq of existing permissions, and removing permissions.
Updating and removing require the Permission ID to be known, so it is
recommended to use \(dq\f[CR]read,write\f[R]\(dq instead of
\(dq\f[CR]write\f[R]\(dq if you wish to update/remove permissions.
.PP
Permissions are read/written in JSON format using the same schema as the
\c
.UR https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/onedrive/developer/rest-api/resources/permission?view=odsp-graph-online
OneDrive API
.UE \c
, which differs slightly between OneDrive Personal and Business.
.PP
Example for OneDrive Personal:
.IP
.EX
[
    {
        \(dqid\(dq: \(dq1234567890ABC!123\(dq,
        \(dqgrantedTo\(dq: {
            \(dquser\(dq: {
                \(dqid\(dq: \(dqryan\(atcontoso.com\(dq
            },
            \(dqapplication\(dq: {},
            \(dqdevice\(dq: {}
        },
        \(dqinvitation\(dq: {
            \(dqemail\(dq: \(dqryan\(atcontoso.com\(dq
        },
        \(dqlink\(dq: {
            \(dqwebUrl\(dq: \(dqhttps://1drv.ms/t/s!1234567890ABC\(dq
        },
        \(dqroles\(dq: [
            \(dqread\(dq
        ],
        \(dqshareId\(dq: \(dqs!1234567890ABC\(dq
    }
]
.EE
.PP
Example for OneDrive Business:
.IP
.EX
[
    {
        \(dqid\(dq: \(dq48d31887\-5fad\-4d73\-a9f5\-3c356e68a038\(dq,
        \(dqgrantedToIdentities\(dq: [
            {
                \(dquser\(dq: {
                    \(dqdisplayName\(dq: \(dqryan\(atcontoso.com\(dq
                },
                \(dqapplication\(dq: {},
                \(dqdevice\(dq: {}
            }
        ],
        \(dqlink\(dq: {
            \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqview\(dq,
            \(dqscope\(dq: \(dqusers\(dq,
            \(dqwebUrl\(dq: \(dqhttps://contoso.sharepoint.com/:w:/t/design/a577ghg9hgh737613bmbjf839026561fmzhsr85ng9f3hjck2t5s\(dq
        },
        \(dqroles\(dq: [
            \(dqread\(dq
        ],
        \(dqshareId\(dq: \(dqu!LKj1lkdlals90j1nlkascl\(dq
    },
    {
        \(dqid\(dq: \(dq5D33DD65C6932946\(dq,
        \(dqgrantedTo\(dq: {
            \(dquser\(dq: {
                \(dqdisplayName\(dq: \(dqJohn Doe\(dq,
                \(dqid\(dq: \(dqefee1b77\-fb3b\-4f65\-99d6\-274c11914d12\(dq
            },
            \(dqapplication\(dq: {},
            \(dqdevice\(dq: {}
        },
        \(dqroles\(dq: [
            \(dqowner\(dq
        ],
        \(dqshareId\(dq: \(dqFWxc1lasfdbEAGM5fI7B67aB5ZMPDMmQ11U\(dq
    }
]
.EE
.PP
To write permissions, pass in a \(dqpermissions\(dq metadata key using
this same format.
The \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#metadata-mapper
\f[CR]\-\-metadata\-mapper\f[R]
.UE \c
\ tool can be very helpful for this.
.PP
When adding permissions, an email address can be provided in the
\f[CR]User.ID\f[R] or \f[CR]DisplayName\f[R] properties of
\f[CR]grantedTo\f[R] or \f[CR]grantedToIdentities\f[R].
Alternatively, an ObjectID can be provided in \f[CR]User.ID\f[R].
At least one valid recipient must be provided in order to add a
permission for a user.
Creating a Public Link is also supported, if \f[CR]Link.Scope\f[R] is
set to \f[CR]\(dqanonymous\(dq\f[R].
.PP
Example request to add a \(dqread\(dq permission with
\f[CR]\-\-metadata\-mapper\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqMetadata\(dq: {
        \(dqpermissions\(dq: \(dq[{\(rs\(dqgrantedToIdentities\(rs\(dq:[{\(rs\(dquser\(rs\(dq:{\(rs\(dqid\(rs\(dq:\(rs\(dqryan\(atcontoso.com\(rs\(dq}}],\(rs\(dqroles\(rs\(dq:[\(rs\(dqread\(rs\(dq]}]\(dq
    }
}
.EE
.PP
Note that adding a permission can fail if a conflicting permission
already exists for the file/folder.
.PP
To update an existing permission, include both the Permission ID and the
new \f[CR]roles\f[R] to be assigned.
\f[CR]roles\f[R] is the only property that can be changed.
.PP
To remove permissions, pass in a blob containing only the permissions
you wish to keep (which can be empty, to remove all.)
Note that the \f[CR]owner\f[R] role will be ignored, as it cannot be
removed.
.PP
Note that both reading and writing permissions requires extra API calls,
so if you don\(aqt need to read or write permissions it is recommended
to omit \f[CR]\-\-onedrive\-metadata\-permissions\f[R].
.PP
Metadata and permissions are supported for Folders (directories) as well
as Files.
Note that setting the \f[CR]mtime\f[R] or \f[CR]btime\f[R] on a Folder
requires one extra API call on OneDrive Business only.
.PP
OneDrive does not currently support User Metadata.
When writing metadata, only writeable system properties will be written
\-\- any read\-only or unrecognized keys passed in will be ignored.
.PP
TIP: to see the metadata and permissions for any file or folder, run:
.IP
.EX
rclone lsjson remote:path \-\-stat \-M \-\-onedrive\-metadata\-permissions read
.EE
.PP
Here are the possible system metadata items for the onedrive backend.
