.SS Limitations
Note that OpenDrive is case insensitive so you can\(aqt have a file
called \(dqHello.doc\(dq and one called \(dqhello.doc\(dq.
.PP
There are quite a few characters that can\(aqt be in OpenDrive file
names.
These can\(aqt occur on Windows platforms, but on non\-Windows platforms
they are common.
Rclone will map these names to and from an identical looking unicode
equivalent.
For example if a file has a \f[CR]?\f[R] in it will be mapped to
\f[CR]？\f[R] instead.
.PP
\f[CR]rclone about\f[R] is not supported by the OpenDrive backend.
Backends without this capability cannot determine free space for an
rclone mount or use policy \f[CR]mfs\f[R] (most free space) as a member
of an rclone union remote.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#optional-features
List of backends that do not support rclone about
.UE \c
\ and \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_about/
