.SS Backend commands
Here are the commands specific to the oracleobjectstorage backend.
.PP
Run them with:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend COMMAND remote:
.EE
.PP
The help below will explain what arguments each command takes.
.PP
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/commands/rclone_backend/
backend
.UE \c
\ command for more info on how to pass options and arguments.
.PP
These can be run on a running backend using the rc command \c
.UR https://rclone.org/rc/#backend-command
backend/command
.UE \c
\&.
.SS rename
change the name of an object.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend rename remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command can be used to rename a object.
.PP
Usage example:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend rename oos:bucket relative\-object\-path\-under\-bucket object\-new\-name
.EE
.SS list\-multipart\-uploads
List the unfinished multipart uploads.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend list\-multipart\-uploads remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command lists the unfinished multipart uploads in JSON format.
.PP
Usage example:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend list\-multipart\-uploads oos:bucket/path/to/object
.EE
.PP
It returns a dictionary of buckets with values as lists of unfinished
multipart uploads.
.PP
You can call it with no bucket in which case it lists all bucket, with a
bucket or with a bucket and path.
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqtest\-bucket\(dq: [
        {
            \(dqnamespace\(dq: \(dqtest\-namespace\(dq,
            \(dqbucket\(dq: \(dqtest\-bucket\(dq,
            \(dqobject\(dq: \(dq600m.bin\(dq,
            \(dquploadId\(dq: \(dq51dd8114\-52a4\-b2f2\-c42f\-5291f05eb3c8\(dq,
            \(dqtimeCreated\(dq: \(dq2022\-07\-29T06:21:16.595Z\(dq,
            \(dqstorageTier\(dq: \(dqStandard\(dq
        }
    ]
}

\f[B]###\f[R] \f[B]cleanup\f[R]

\f[B]Remove\f[R] \f[B]unfinished\f[R] \f[B]multipart\f[R] \f[B]uploads.\f[R]

\f[B]\(ga\(ga\(gaconsole\f[R]
\f[B]rclone\f[R] \f[B]backend\f[R] \f[B]cleanup\f[R] \f[B]remote:\f[R] [\f[B]options\f[R]] [\f[B]<arguments>+\f[R]]
.EE
.PP
This command removes unfinished multipart uploads of age greater than
max\-age which defaults to 24 hours.
.PP
Note that you can use \-\-interactive/\-i or \-\-dry\-run with this
command to see what it would do.
.PP
Usage examples:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend cleanup oos:bucket/path/to/object
rclone backend cleanup \-o max\-age=7w oos:bucket/path/to/object
.EE
.PP
Durations are parsed as per the rest of rclone, 2h, 7d, 7w etc.
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqmax\-age\(dq: Max age of upload to delete.
.SS restore
Restore objects from Archive to Standard storage.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend restore remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command can be used to restore one or more objects from Archive to
Standard storage.
.PP
Usage examples:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend restore oos:bucket/path/to/directory \-o hours=HOURS
rclone backend restore oos:bucket \-o hours=HOURS
.EE
.PP
This flag also obeys the filters.
Test first with \-\-interactive/\-i or \-\-dry\-run flags
.IP
.EX
rclone \-\-interactive backend restore \-\-include \(dq*.txt\(dq oos:bucket/path \-o hours=72
.EE
.PP
All the objects shown will be marked for restore, then:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend restore \-\-include \(dq*.txt\(dq oos:bucket/path \-o hours=72
.EE
.PP
It returns a list of status dictionaries with Object Name and Status
keys.
The Status will be \(dqRESTORED\(dq\(dq if it was successful or an error
message if not.
.IP
.EX
[
    {
        \(dqObject\(dq: \(dqtest.txt\(dq
        \(dqStatus\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dqRESTORED\(dq,
    },
    {
        \(dqObject\(dq: \(dqtest/file4.txt\(dq
        \(dqStatus\(dq\f[B]:\f[R] \(dqRESTORED\(dq,
    }
]
.EE
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqhours\(dq: The number of hours for which this object will be
restored.
Default is 24 hrs.
.SS Tutorials
.SS \c
.UR https://rclone.org/oracleobjectstorage/tutorial_mount/
Mounting Buckets
.UE \c
.SH QingStor
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:bucket\f[R] (or \f[CR]remote:\f[R]
for the \f[CR]lsd\f[R] command.)
You may put subdirectories in too, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:bucket/path/to/dir\f[R].
.SS Configuration
Here is an example of making an QingStor configuration.
First run
.IP
.EX
rclone config
.EE
.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process.
.IP
.EX
