.EE
.PP
This remote is called \f[CR]remote\f[R] and can now be used like this
.PP
See all buckets
.IP
.EX
rclone lsd remote:
.EE
.PP
Make a new bucket
.IP
.EX
rclone mkdir remote:bucket
.EE
.PP
List the contents of a bucket
.IP
.EX
rclone ls remote:bucket
.EE
.PP
Sync \f[CR]/home/local/directory\f[R] to the remote bucket, deleting any
excess files in the bucket.
.IP
.EX
rclone sync \-\-interactive /home/local/directory remote:bucket
.EE
.SS \-\-fast\-list
This remote supports \f[CR]\-\-fast\-list\f[R] which allows you to use
fewer transactions in exchange for more memory.
See the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#fast-list
rclone docs
.UE \c
\ for more details.
.SS Multipart uploads
rclone supports multipart uploads with QingStor which means that it can
upload files bigger than 5 GiB.
Note that files uploaded with multipart upload don\(aqt have an MD5SUM.
.PP
Note that incomplete multipart uploads older than 24 hours can be
removed with \f[CR]rclone cleanup remote:bucket\f[R] just for one bucket
\f[CR]rclone cleanup remote:\f[R] for all buckets.
QingStor does not ever remove incomplete multipart uploads so it may be
necessary to run this from time to time.
.SS Buckets and Zone
With QingStor you can list buckets (\f[CR]rclone lsd\f[R]) using any
zone, but you can only access the content of a bucket from the zone it
was created in.
If you attempt to access a bucket from the wrong zone, you will get an
error, \f[CR]incorrect zone, the bucket is not in \(aqXXX\(aq zone\f[R].
.SS Authentication
There are two ways to supply \f[CR]rclone\f[R] with a set of QingStor
credentials.
In order of precedence:
.IP \(bu 2
Directly in the rclone configuration file (as configured by
\f[CR]rclone config\f[R])
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
set \f[CR]access_key_id\f[R] and \f[CR]secret_access_key\f[R]
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Runtime configuration:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
set \f[CR]env_auth\f[R] to \f[CR]true\f[R] in the config file
.IP \(bu 2
Exporting the following environment variables before running
\f[CR]rclone\f[R]
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
Access Key ID: \f[CR]QS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\f[R] or \f[CR]QS_ACCESS_KEY\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Secret Access Key: \f[CR]QS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\f[R] or
\f[CR]QS_SECRET_KEY\f[R]
.RE
.RE
.SS Restricted filename characters
The control characters 0x00\-0x1F and / are replaced as in the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#restricted-characters
default restricted characters set
.UE \c
\&.
Note that 0x7F is not replaced.
.PP
Invalid UTF\-8 bytes will also be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
, as they can\(aqt be used in JSON strings.
