.SS Storage usage
The storage usage in Quatrix is restricted to the account during the
purchase.
You can restrict any user with a smaller storage limit.
The account limit is applied if the user has no custom storage limit.
Once you\(aqve reached the limit, the upload of files will fail.
This can be fixed by freeing up the space or increasing the quota.
.SS Server\-side operations
Quatrix supports server\-side operations (copy and move).
In case of conflict, files are overwritten during server\-side
operation.
.SH Sia
Sia (\c
.UR https://sia.tech/
sia.tech
.UE \c
) is a decentralized cloud storage platform based on the \c
.UR https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockchain
blockchain
.UE \c
\ technology.
With rclone you can use it like any other remote filesystem or mount Sia
folders locally.
The technology behind it involves a number of new concepts such as
Siacoins and Wallet, Blockchain and Consensus, Renting and Hosting, and
so on.
If you are new to it, you\(aqd better first familiarize yourself using
their excellent \c
.UR https://support.sia.tech/
support documentation
.UE \c
\&.
.SS Introduction
Before you can use rclone with Sia, you will need to have a running copy
of \f[CR]Sia\-UI\f[R] or \f[CR]siad\f[R] (the Sia daemon) locally on
your computer or on local network (e.g.
a NAS).
Please follow the \c
.UR https://sia.tech/get-started
Get started
.UE \c
\ guide and install one.
.PP
rclone interacts with Sia network by talking to the Sia daemon via \c
.UR https://docs.sia.tech/
HTTP API
.UE \c
\ which is usually available on port \f[I]9980\f[R].
By default you will run the daemon locally on the same computer so
it\(aqs safe to leave the API password blank (the API URL will be
\f[CR]http://127.0.0.1:9980\f[R] making external access impossible).
.PP
However, if you want to access Sia daemon running on another node, for
example due to memory constraints or because you want to share single
daemon between several rclone and Sia\-UI instances, you\(aqll need to
make a few more provisions:
.IP \(bu 2
Ensure you have \f[I]Sia daemon\f[R] installed directly or in a \c
.UR https://github.com/SiaFoundation/siad/pkgs/container/siad
docker container
.UE \c
\ because Sia\-UI does not support this mode natively.
.IP \(bu 2
Run it on externally accessible port, for example provide
\f[CR]\-\-api\-addr :9980\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-disable\-api\-security\f[R]
arguments on the daemon command line.
.IP \(bu 2
Enforce API password for the \f[CR]siad\f[R] daemon via environment
variable \f[CR]SIA_API_PASSWORD\f[R] or text file named
\f[CR]apipassword\f[R] in the daemon directory.
.IP \(bu 2
Set rclone backend option \f[CR]api_password\f[R] taking it from above
locations.
.PP
Notes:
.IP "1." 3
If your wallet is locked, rclone cannot unlock it automatically.
You should either unlock it in advance by using Sia\-UI or via command
line \f[CR]siac wallet unlock\f[R].
Alternatively you can make \f[CR]siad\f[R] unlock your wallet
automatically upon startup by running it with environment variable
\f[CR]SIA_WALLET_PASSWORD\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
If \f[CR]siad\f[R] cannot find the \f[CR]SIA_API_PASSWORD\f[R] variable
or the \f[CR]apipassword\f[R] file in the \f[CR]SIA_DIR\f[R] directory,
it will generate a random password and store in the text file named
\f[CR]apipassword\f[R] under \f[CR]YOUR_HOME/.sia/\f[R] directory on
Unix or
\f[CR]C:\(rsUsers\(rsYOUR_HOME\(rsAppData\(rsLocal\(rsSia\(rsapipassword\f[R]
on Windows.
Remember this when you configure password in rclone.
.IP "3." 3
The only way to use \f[CR]siad\f[R] without API password is to run it
\f[B]on localhost\f[R] with command line argument
\f[CR]\-\-authorize\-api=false\f[R], but this is insecure and
\f[B]strongly discouraged\f[R].
