.SS addurl
Add offline download task for url.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend addurl remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command adds offline download task for url.
.PP
Usage examples:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend addurl pikpak:dirpath url
rclone backend addurl pikpak:dirpath url \-o name=custom_filename.zip
.EE
.PP
Downloads will be stored in \(aqdirpath\(aq.
If \(aqdirpath\(aq is invalid, download will fallback to default \(aqMy
Pack\(aq folder.
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqname\(dq: Custom filename for the downloaded file.
.SS decompress
Request decompress of a file/files in a folder.
.IP
.EX
rclone backend decompress remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE
.PP
This command requests decompress of file/files in a folder.
.PP
Usage examples:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend decompress pikpak:dirpath {filename} \-o password=password
rclone backend decompress pikpak:dirpath {filename} \-o delete\-src\-file
.EE
.PP
An optional argument \(aqfilename\(aq can be specified for a file
located in \(aqpikpak:dirpath\(aq.
You may want to pass \(aq\-o password=password\(aq for a
password\-protected files.
Also, pass \(aq\-o delete\-src\-file\(aq to delete source files after
decompression finished.
.PP
Result:
.IP
.EX
{
    \(dqDecompressed\(dq: 17,
    \(dqSourceDeleted\(dq: 0,
    \(dqErrors\(dq: 0
}
.EE
.SS Limitations
.SS Hashes may be empty
PikPak supports MD5 hash, but sometimes given empty especially for
user\-uploaded files.
.SS Deleted files still visible with trashed\-only
Deleted files will still be visible with
\f[CR]\-\-pikpak\-trashed\-only\f[R] even after the trash emptied.
This goes away after few days.
