.SS Modification times and hashes
Proton Drive Bridge does not support updating modification times yet.
.PP
The SHA1 hash algorithm is supported.
.SS Restricted filename characters
Invalid UTF\-8 bytes will be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
, also left and right spaces will be removed (\c
.UR https://github.com/ProtonMail/WebClients/blob/b4eba99d241af4fdae06ff7138bd651a40ef5d3c/applications/drive/src/app/store/_links/validation.ts#L51
code reference
.UE \c
)
.SS Duplicated files
Proton Drive can not have two files with exactly the same name and path.
If the conflict occurs, depending on the advanced config, the file might
or might not be overwritten.
.SS \c
.UR https://proton.me/support/the-difference-between-the-mailbox-password-and-login-password
Mailbox password
.UE \c
Please set your mailbox password in the advanced config section.
.SS Caching
The cache is currently built for the case when the rclone is the only
instance performing operations to the mount point.
The event system, which is the proton API system that provides
visibility of what has changed on the drive, is yet to be implemented,
so updates from other clients won\(cqt be reflected in the cache.
Thus, if there are concurrent clients accessing the same mount point,
then we might have a problem with caching the stale data.
