.SS \-\-sftp\-path\-override
Override path used by SSH shell commands.
.PP
This allows checksum calculation when SFTP and SSH paths are different.
This issue affects among others Synology NAS boxes.
.PP
E.g.
if shared folders can be found in directories representing volumes:
.IP
.EX
rclone sync /home/local/directory remote:/directory \-\-sftp\-path\-override /volume2/directory
.EE
.PP
E.g.
if home directory can be found in a shared folder called \(dqhome\(dq:
.IP
.EX
rclone sync /home/local/directory remote:/home/directory \-\-sftp\-path\-override /volume1/homes/USER/directory
.EE
.PP
To specify only the path to the SFTP remote\(aqs root, and allow rclone
to add any relative subpaths automatically (including
unwrapping/decrypting remotes as necessary), add the \(aq\(at\(aq
character to the beginning of the path.
.PP
E.g.
the first example above could be rewritten as:
.IP
.EX
rclone sync /home/local/directory remote:/directory \-\-sftp\-path\-override \(at/volume2
.EE
.PP
Note that when using this method with Synology \(dqhome\(dq folders, the
full \(dq/homes/USER\(dq path should be specified instead of
\(dq/home\(dq.
.PP
E.g.
the second example above should be rewritten as:
.IP
.EX
rclone sync /home/local/directory remote:/homes/USER/directory \-\-sftp\-path\-override \(at/volume1
.EE
.PP
