.SS Limitations
On some SFTP servers (e.g.
Synology) the paths are different for SSH and SFTP so the hashes
can\(aqt be calculated properly.
You can either use \f[CR]\-\-sftp\-path\-override\f[R] or
\f[CR]disable_hashcheck\f[R].
.PP
The only ssh agent supported under Windows is Putty\(aqs pageant.
.PP
The Go SSH library disables the use of the aes128\-cbc cipher by
default, due to security concerns.
This can be re\-enabled on a per\-connection basis by setting the
\f[CR]use_insecure_cipher\f[R] setting in the configuration file to
\f[CR]true\f[R].
Further details on the insecurity of this cipher can be found \c
.UR http://www.isg.rhul.ac.uk/~kp/SandPfinal.pdf
in this paper
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
SFTP isn\(aqt supported under plan9 until \c
.UR https://github.com/pkg/sftp/issues/156
this issue
.UE \c
\ is fixed.
.PP
Note that since SFTP isn\(aqt HTTP based the following flags don\(aqt
work with it: \f[CR]\-\-dump headers\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dump bodies\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-dump auth\f[R].
.PP
Note that \f[CR]\-\-timeout\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-contimeout\f[R] are both
supported.
.SS rsync.net
rsync.net is supported through the SFTP backend.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://www.rsync.net/products/rclone.html
rsync.net\(aqs documentation of rclone examples
.UE \c
\&.
.SS Hetzner Storage Box
Hetzner Storage Boxes are supported through the SFTP backend on port 23.
.PP
See \c
.UR https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/storage-box/access/access-ssh-rsync-borg#rclone
Hetzner\(aqs documentation for details
.UE \c
.SH Shade
This is a backend for the \c
.UR https://shade.inc/
Shade
.UE \c
\ platform
.SS About Shade
\c
.UR https://shade.inc/
Shade
.UE \c
\ is an AI\-powered cloud NAS that makes your cloud files behave like a
local drive, optimized for media and creative workflows.
It provides fast, secure access with natural\-language search, easy
sharing, and scalable cloud storage.
.SS Accounts & Pricing
To use this backend, you need to \c
.UR https://app.shade.inc/
create a free account
.UE \c
\ on Shade.
You can start with a free account and get 20GB of storage for free.
.SS Usage
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:path\f[R]
.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:directory/subdirectory\f[R].
.SS Configuration
Here is an example of making a Shade configuration.
.PP
First, create a \c
.UR https://app.shade.inc/
create a free account
.UE \c
\ account and choose a plan.
.PP
You will need to log in and get the \f[CR]API Key\f[R] and
\f[CR]Drive ID\f[R] for your account from the settings section of your
account and created drive respectively.
.PP
Now run
.PP
\f[CR]rclone config\f[R]
.PP
