.SH SMB
SMB is \c
.UR https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Server_Message_Block
a communication protocol to share files over network
.UE \c
\&.
.PP
This relies on \c
.UR https://github.com/CloudSoda/go-smb2/
go\-smb2 library
.UE \c
\ for communication with SMB protocol.
.PP
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:sharename\f[R] (or
\f[CR]remote:\f[R] for the \f[CR]lsd\f[R] command.)
You may put subdirectories in too, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:item/path/to/dir\f[R].
.SS Notes
The first path segment must be the name of the share, which you entered
when you started to share on Windows.
On smbd, it\(aqs the section title in \f[CR]smb.conf\f[R] (usually in
\f[CR]/etc/samba/\f[R]) file.
You can find shares by querying the root if you\(aqre unsure (e.g.
\f[CR]rclone lsd remote:\f[R]).
.PP
You can\(aqt access the shared printers from rclone, obviously.
.PP
You can\(aqt use Anonymous access for logging in.
You have to use the \f[CR]guest\f[R] user with an empty password
instead.
The rclone client tries to avoid 8.3 names when uploading files by
encoding trailing spaces and periods.
Alternatively, \c
.UR https://rclone.org/local/#paths-on-windows
the local backend
.UE \c
\ on Windows can access SMB servers using UNC paths, by
\f[CR]\(rs\(rsserver\(rsshare\f[R].
This doesn\(aqt apply to non\-Windows OSes, such as Linux and macOS.
