List all the files in your SugarSync folder \(dqTest\(dq
.IP
.EX
rclone ls remote:Test
.EE
.PP
To copy a local directory to an SugarSync folder called backup
.IP
.EX
rclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE
.PP
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:path\f[R]
.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:directory/subdirectory\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]NB\f[R] you can\(aqt create files in the top level folder you have
to create a folder, which rclone will create as a \(dqSync Folder\(dq
with SugarSync.
.SS Modification times and hashes
SugarSync does not support modification times or hashes, therefore
syncing will default to \f[CR]\-\-size\-only\f[R] checking.
Note that using \f[CR]\-\-update\f[R] will work as rclone can read the
time files were uploaded.
.SS Restricted filename characters
SugarSync replaces the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#restricted-characters
default restricted characters set
.UE \c
\ except for DEL.
.PP
Invalid UTF\-8 bytes will also be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
, as they can\(aqt be used in XML strings.
.SS Deleting files
Deleted files will be moved to the \(dqDeleted items\(dq folder by
default.
.PP
However you can supply the flag \f[CR]\-\-sugarsync\-hard\-delete\f[R]
or set the config parameter \f[CR]hard_delete = true\f[R] if you would
like files to be deleted straight away.
