.SH TelDrive
TelDrive is a self\-hosted file storage solution that uses Telegram
channels as the underlying storage backend.
Files are split into chunks, optionally encrypted, and uploaded as
messages in a designated Telegram channel or group.
The TelDrive API server indexes and manages the file metadata, providing
a file\-system\-like interface over Telegram\(aqs storage.
.PP
Paths are specified as \f[CR]remote:path\f[R].
.PP
To use TelDrive, you need:
.IP \(bu 2
A running TelDrive server (self\-hosted)
.IP \(bu 2
An API key for authentication
.SS Filesystem behavior
TelDrive uses case\-sensitive names, matching the normal behavior of
Linux filesystems.
For example, \f[CR]Photo.jpg\f[R] and \f[CR]photo.jpg\f[R] are distinct
files in the same directory.
.PP
Directory listings are delivered page by page.
Failed multipart uploads automatically reuse an exact\-compatible open
TelDrive upload session and skip parts that the server has already
stored.
Compatibility includes destination, exact\-case name, size, MIME type,
modification time, encryption mode, conflict policy, and BLAKE3 hash
when the source provides one.
.PP
Deleting a file or directory moves it to TelDrive trash.
Use \f[CR]rclone cleanup remote:\f[R] to permanently purge all
top\-level trashed entries under the configured remote root.
Individual entries can be managed by ID:
.IP
.EX
rclone backend trash\-list remote:
rclone backend restore remote: FILE_ID
rclone backend purge remote: FILE_ID
.EE
.SS Configuration
