.PP
Once configured you can then use \f[CR]rclone\f[R] like this (replace
\f[CR]remote\f[R] with the name you gave your remote):
.PP
List folders in root level folder:
.IP
.EX
rclone lsd remote:
.EE
.PP
List all the files in your root folder:
.IP
.EX
rclone ls remote:
.EE
.PP
To copy a local folder to a Uloz.to folder called backup:
.IP
.EX
rclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE
.SS User credentials
The only reliable method is to authenticate the user using username and
password.
Uloz.to offers an API key as well, but it\(aqs reserved for the use of
Uloz.to\(aqs in\-house application and using it in different
circumstances is unreliable.
.SS Modification times and hashes
Uloz.to doesn\(aqt allow the user to set a custom modification time, or
retrieve the hashes after upload.
As a result, the integration uses a free form field the API provides to
encode client\-provided timestamps and hashes.
Timestamps are stored with microsecond precision.
.PP
A server calculated MD5 hash of the file is verified upon upload.
Afterwards, the backend only serves the client\-side calculated hashes.
Hashes can also be retrieved upon creating a file download link, but
it\(aqs impractical for \f[CR]list\f[R]\-like use cases.
.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#restricted-characters
default restricted characters set
.UE \c
\ the following characters are also replaced:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l c c.
T{
Character
T}@T{
Value
T}@T{
Replacement
T}
_
T{
\(rs
T}@T{
0x5C
T}@T{
＼
T}
.TE
.PP
Invalid UTF\-8 bytes will also be \c
.UR https://rclone.org/overview/#invalid-utf8
replaced
.UE \c
, as they can\(aqt be used in JSON strings.
.SS Transfers
All files are currently uploaded using a single HTTP request, so for
uploading large files a stable connection is necessary.
Rclone will upload up to \f[CR]\-\-transfers\f[R] chunks at the same
time (shared among all uploads).
.SS Deleting files
By default, files are moved to the recycle bin whereas folders are
deleted immediately.
Trashed files are permanently deleted after 30 days in the recycle bin.
.PP
Emptying the trash is currently not implemented in rclone.
.SS Root folder ID
You can set the \f[CR]root_folder_slug\f[R] for rclone.
This is the folder (identified by its \f[CR]Folder slug\f[R]) that
rclone considers to be the root of your Uloz.to drive.
.PP
Normally you will leave this blank and rclone will determine the correct
root to use itself.
However you can set this to restrict rclone to a specific folder
hierarchy.
.PP
In order to do this you will have to find the \f[CR]Folder slug\f[R] of
the folder you wish to use as root.
This will be the last segment of the URL when you open the relevant
folder in the Uloz.to web interface.
.PP
For example, for exploring a folder with URL
\f[CR]https://uloz.to/fm/my\-files/foobar\f[R], \f[CR]foobar\f[R] should
be used as the root slug.
.PP
\f[CR]root_folder_slug\f[R] can be used alongside a specific path in the
remote path.
For example, if your remote\(aqs \f[CR]root_folder_slug\f[R] corresponds
to \f[CR]/foo/bar\f[R], \f[CR]remote:baz/qux\f[R] will refer to
\f[CR]ABSOLUTE_ULOZTO_ROOT/foo/bar/baz/qux\f[R].
