.SS \-\-yandex\-upload\-wait
Wait this long after an upload before setting the modification time.
.PP
Yandex Disk finalizes an upload asynchronously on its servers after the
upload has completed.
If the modification time is set while this finalization is still in
progress the server returns 500 Internal Server Error errors.
.PP
If you are getting 500 errors on upload then setting this to 2s is
normally enough to stop them, at the cost of slowing down uploads.
.PP
Yandex support recommend a value of 1.5s \- 3s.
.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config: upload_wait
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var: RCLONE_YANDEX_UPLOAD_WAIT
.IP \(bu 2
Type: Duration
.IP \(bu 2
Default: 0s
.SS \-\-yandex\-description
Description of the remote.
.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config: description
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var: RCLONE_YANDEX_DESCRIPTION
.IP \(bu 2
Type: string
.IP \(bu 2
Required: false
.SS Limitations
When uploading very large files (bigger than about 5 GiB) you will need
to increase the \f[CR]\-\-timeout\f[R] parameter.
This is because Yandex pauses (perhaps to calculate the MD5SUM for the
entire file) before returning confirmation that the file has been
uploaded.
The default handling of timeouts in rclone is to assume a 5 minute pause
is an error and close the connection \- you\(aqll see
\f[CR]net/http: timeout awaiting response headers\f[R] errors in the
logs if this is happening.
Setting the timeout to twice the max size of file in GiB should be
enough, so if you want to upload a 30 GiB file set a timeout of
\f[CR]2 * 30 = 60m\f[R], that is \f[CR]\-\-timeout 60m\f[R].
.PP
If you get \f[CR]500 Internal Server Error\f[R] errors just after
uploads, particularly when uploading many files in parallel, then try
setting \f[CR]\-\-yandex\-upload\-wait 2s\f[R].
Yandex Disk finalizes uploads asynchronously on its servers and can
report an upload as complete slightly before the file is ready, so
accessing the file\(aqs metadata too soon causes these errors.
Yandex support recommend waiting 1.5s \- 3s after each upload.
.PP
Having a Yandex Mail account is mandatory to use the Yandex.Disk
subscription.
Token generation will work without a mail account, but Rclone won\(aqt
be able to complete any actions.
.IP
.EX
[403 \- DiskUnsupportedUserAccountTypeError] User account type is not supported.
.EE
