.SS Setting up your own client_id
For Zoho we advise you to set up your own client_id.
To do so you have to complete the following steps.
.IP "1." 3
Log in to the \c
.UR https://api-console.zoho.com
Zoho API Console
.UE \c
.IP "2." 3
Create a new client of type \(dqServer\-based Application\(dq.
The name and website don\(aqt matter, but you must add the redirect URL
\f[CR]http://localhost:53682/\f[R].
.IP "3." 3
Once the client is created, you can go to the settings tab and enable it
in other regions.
.PP
The client id and client secret can now be used with rclone.
.SH Local Filesystem
Local paths are specified as normal filesystem paths, e.g.
\f[CR]/path/to/wherever\f[R], so
.IP
.EX
rclone sync \-\-interactive /home/source /tmp/destination
.EE
.PP
Will sync \f[CR]/home/source\f[R] to \f[CR]/tmp/destination\f[R].
.SS Configuration
For consistencies sake one can also configure a remote of type
\f[CR]local\f[R] in the config file, and access the local filesystem
using rclone remote paths, e.g.
\f[CR]remote:path/to/wherever\f[R], but it is probably easier not to.
.SS Modification times
Rclone reads and writes the modification times using an accuracy
determined by the OS.
Typically this is 1ns on Linux, 10 ns on Windows and 1 Second on OS X.
.SS Filenames
Filenames should be encoded in UTF\-8 on disk.
This is the normal case for Windows and OS X.
.PP
There is a bit more uncertainty in the Linux world, but new
distributions will have UTF\-8 encoded files names.
If you are using an old Linux filesystem with non UTF\-8 file names
(e.g.
latin1) then you can use the \f[CR]convmv\f[R] tool to convert the
filesystem to UTF\-8.
This tool is available in most distributions\(aq package managers.
.PP
If an invalid (non\-UTF8) filename is read, the invalid characters will
be replaced with a quoted representation of the invalid bytes.
The name \f[CR]gro\(rsxdf\f[R] will be transferred as \f[CR]gro‛DF\f[R].
\f[CR]rclone\f[R] will emit a debug message in this case (use
\f[CR]\-v\f[R] to see), e.g.
.IP
.EX
Local file system at .: Replacing invalid UTF\-8 characters in \(dqgro\(rsxdf\(dq
.EE
.SS Restricted characters
With the local backend, restrictions on the characters that are usable
in file or directory names depend on the operating system.
To check what rclone will replace by default on your system, run
\f[CR]rclone help flags local\-encoding\f[R].
.PP
