.SS Metadata
Depending on which OS is in use the local backend may return only some
of the system metadata.
Setting system metadata is supported on all OSes but setting user
metadata is only supported on linux, freebsd, netbsd, macOS and Solaris.
It is \f[B]not\f[R] supported on Windows yet (\c
.UR https://github.com/pkg/xattr/issues/47
see pkg/attrs#47
.UE \c
).
.PP
User metadata is stored as extended attributes (which may not be
supported by all file systems) under the \(dquser.*\(dq prefix.
.PP
Metadata is supported on files and directories.
.PP
When restoring metadata with \f[CR]\-\-metadata\f[R] rclone applies the
\(dqmode\(dq, \(dquid\(dq and \(dqgid\(dq from the source.
These come from the source remote which may not be trusted, so restoring
metadata as root from an untrusted source can change file ownership and
is not recommended.
The setuid, setgid and sticky bits are not restored by default \- see
the \f[CR]\-\-local\-metadata\-restore\-special\-bits\f[R] flag.
.PP
