\f[CR]\-\-track\-renames\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-backup\-dir\f[R] are now
supported (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Final listings are now generated from sync results, to avoid needing to
re\-list (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync is now much more resilient to changes that happen during a bisync
run, and far less prone to critical errors / undetected changes
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync is now capable of rolling a file listing back in cases of
uncertainty, essentially marking the file as needing to be rechecked
next time.
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A few basic terminal colors are now supported, controllable with \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#color-autoneveralways
\f[CR]\-\-color\f[R]
.UE \c
\ (\f[CR]AUTO\f[R]|\f[CR]NEVER\f[R]|\f[CR]ALWAYS\f[R]) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Initial listing snapshots of Path1 and Path2 are now generated
concurrently, using the same \(dqmarch\(dq infrastructure as
\f[CR]check\f[R] and \f[CR]sync\f[R], for performance improvements and
less risk of error.
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-resync\f[R] is now much more efficient (especially for users
of \f[CR]\-\-create\-empty\-src\-dirs\f[R]) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Google Docs (and other files of unknown size) are now supported (with
the same options as in \f[CR]sync\f[R]) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Equality checks before a sync conflict rename now fall back to
\f[CR]cryptcheck\f[R] (when possible) or \f[CR]\-\-download\f[R],
(nielash) instead of of \f[CR]\-\-size\-only\f[R], when \f[CR]check\f[R]
is not available.
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now fully supports comparing based on any combination of size,
modtime, and checksum, lifting the prior restriction on backends without
modtime support.
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports a \(dqGraceful Shutdown\(dq mode to cleanly cancel a
run early without requiring \f[CR]\-\-resync\f[R].
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
New \f[CR]\-\-recover\f[R] flag allows robust recovery in the event of
interruptions, without requiring \f[CR]\-\-resync\f[R].
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A new \f[CR]\-\-max\-lock\f[R] setting allows lock files to
automatically renew and expire, for better automatic recovery when a run
is interrupted.
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports auto\-resolving sync conflicts and customizing
rename behavior with new \f[CR]\-\-conflict\-resolve\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-conflict\-loser\f[R], and \f[CR]\-\-conflict\-suffix\f[R]
flags.
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A new \f[CR]\-\-resync\-mode\f[R] flag allows more control over which
version of a file gets kept during a \f[CR]\-\-resync\f[R].
(nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports \c
.UR https://rclone.org/docs/#retries-int
\f[CR]\-\-retries\f[R]
.UE \c
\ and \f[CR]\-\-retries\-sleep\f[R] (when \f[CR]\-\-resilient\f[R] is
set.)
(nielash)
